`β ≠ 0` is not proved (Part XV shows that it vanishes at `β = 0`); Part XXXVI bounds it for `|β| < 1/18`
(`su2_mixed_block`). Part XXVII proves `ker Π ≠ 0` for straight
blocking, every `M ≥ 1` and every real `β` (Part VI proves `H ≠ 0`, and `Y ≠ 0` for `M ≥ 2`; Part XXVII adds
`Y ≠ 0` at `M = 1`), so the bounds on `ker Π` in this file (`hFibre`, `hcons`, the sweep hypothesis, Part XXXVI's fibre Poincaré
inequality) concern a
nonzero space; this is non-vacuity only, and at `β ≠ 0` those bounds remain conditional on named hypotheses or are
paper bounds, except `hcons`, `hFibre` and the sweep hypothesis for every `M ≥ 1` and `|β| ≤ 1/228` (Parts XXVI, XXXIII and
XXXIV) and the fibre Poincaré inequality for every real `β` (Part XXXVI, `su2_fibrePoincare_Pi`).
The lower bounds on `D` and `D_c` for the Wilson model in this file are spectral gaps of heat-bath (cube-resampling)
