/-! # Part XII. `YangMills.StrongCoupling.ConstrainedFibre`: sweep criteria for the constrained fibre bound `hcons` (new; uses Parts I–IV, VI, X and XI) -/

/-!
# Sweep criteria for the constrained fibre bound `hcons`

## (a) Formal target

Part X reduces `hFibre` to the constrained bound
`hcons : λ ‖u‖² ≤ ∑ₓ wₓ ‖u − P'ₓ u‖²` for `Π u = 0`, with `P'ₓ = P_{Vₓ ∖ Sk}`.
This part gives abstract sufficient conditions for `hcons` in exactly that form.

## (b) What is proved

* `norm_sub_sweepProd_sq_le`: for ANY orthogonal projections `P₁, …, Pₙ` (no commutation needed),
  `‖u − P₁ ⋯ Pₙ u‖² ≤ ∑ᵢ ‖u − Pᵢ u‖²`.
* `sweepProd_isOrthProj` / `sweepProj`: if the projections commute pairwise, the product is an
  orthogonal projection, and `form_sweepProj_le_cubeGen` states `I − ∏ P ≤ ∑ (I − P)` as quadratic
  forms (`⟪u, u − Q u⟫ ≤ ⟪u, cubeGen 1 P u⟫`).
* `hcons_of_sweep_vanish`: if the ordered product of the `P'ₓ` along one duplicate-free list
  vanishes on `ker Π`, then `hcons` holds with `λ = w_min` (`0 ≤ w_min ≤ wₓ`).
* `hcons_of_sweeps`: if `m` pairwise disjoint duplicate-free lists each have a product with
  `‖Q_j u‖ ≤ θ ‖u‖` on `ker Π` (`θ ≤ 1`), then `hcons` holds with `λ = m · w_min · (1 − θ)²`.
* `fibre_of_sweeps`, `su2_hFibre_of_sweeps`: the same, fed into `fibre_of_constrained` and
  `su2_hFibre_of_constrained` of Part X, giving `hFibre` for `D = ∑ₓ wₓ (I − P_{Vₓ})`.
* `wilsonMeasure_zero`: at `κ = 0` the Wilson measure is the product measure.
* `GaussK0.k0_margin`: an exact `k = 0` sector certificate `Q0 ≥ (6/25) G0` for the Gaussian-order
  constrained generator in three dimensions (entries produced outside Lean).
* `mem_cube2_self`, `iUnion_cube2_diff_skel`: the constrained cubes `cube2 M x ∖ Sk` cover every
  non-skeleton link (the geometric step of the `β = 0` argument).

## (c) What remains open

The sweep hypotheses are not verified here for the Wilson measure. At `β = 0` they hold with
`θ = 0` and `m = 2^{d−1}` by the paper argument of the accompanying research notes (product measure:
the `P'ₓ` commute and multiply to `E[· | skeleton] = Π` on `H`); that measure theory is not formalised.
For SU(2), `d = 4`, `0 < |β| < 1/1824` the research notes give a paper proof (Dobrushin estimate for
one systematic sweep of the `2^{d−1}` complementary-parity families, whose blocks partition the
non-skeleton links) of the sweep hypothesis with `θ = r/(1 − r)`, `r = 912|β|`, uniformly in `M`;
it is not formalised here. `hResidual` and `hCoarseGap` are untouched.

## (d) Axioms and checks

Only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound` (the module axiom audit covers every headline
theorem); no
unfinished-proof markers, no new axiom declarations, no native evaluation, no `set_option`.

## (e) Scope

This is not a proof of a mass gap. It gives abstract criteria for the constrained bound `hcons`.
-/

namespace YangMills.StrongCoupling.ConstrainedFibre

open scoped InnerProductSpace
open Finset SchurSplit YangMills.StrongCoupling.CubeSplit YangMills.StrongCoupling.CondExpInputs
  YangMills.StrongCoupling.WilsonCube YangMills.StrongCoupling.WilsonSU2
  YangMills.StrongCoupling.FibreReduction

section Abstract

variable {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℝ H] {ι : Type*}

/-- The ordered product `P_{i₁} ⋯ P_{iₙ}` of the projections along a list `[i₁, …, iₙ]`
(a systematic-scan sweep; `P_{iₙ}` acts first). -/
def sweepProd (P : ι → OrthProj H) (l : List ι) : H →ₗ[ℝ] H := (l.map fun i => (P i).P).prod

theorem sweepProd_nil (P : ι → OrthProj H) (u : H) : sweepProd P [] u = u := rfl

theorem sweepProd_cons (P : ι → OrthProj H) (i : ι) (l : List ι) (u : H) :
    sweepProd P (i :: l) u = (P i).P (sweepProd P l u) := by
  simp [sweepProd, Module.End.mul_apply]

theorem norm_P_sq_le (P : OrthProj H) (x : H) : ‖P.P x‖ ^ 2 ≤ ‖x‖ ^ 2 := by
  have h := P.norm_sq_split x
  nlinarith [sq_nonneg ‖x - P.P x‖]

theorem inner_sub_P_P (P : OrthProj H) (u v : H) : ⟪u - P.P u, P.P v⟫_ℝ = 0 := by
  rw [← P.symm, map_sub, P.idem, sub_self, inner_zero_left]

/-- **The sweep inequality.** For any orthogonal projections (no commutation assumed),
`‖u − P_{i₁} ⋯ P_{iₙ} u‖² ≤ ∑ₖ ‖u − P_{iₖ} u‖²`. -/
theorem norm_sub_sweepProd_sq_le (P : ι → OrthProj H) (u : H) :
    ∀ l : List ι, ‖u - sweepProd P l u‖ ^ 2 ≤ (l.map fun i => ‖u - (P i).P u‖ ^ 2).sum
  | [] => by simp [sweepProd_nil]
  | i :: l => by
    have ih := norm_sub_sweepProd_sq_le P u l
    rw [sweepProd_cons, List.map_cons, List.sum_cons]
    have hdec : u - (P i).P (sweepProd P l u) =
        (u - (P i).P u) + (P i).P (u - sweepProd P l u) := by
      rw [map_sub]; abel
    rw [hdec, norm_add_sq_real, inner_sub_P_P, mul_zero, add_zero]
    have h2 := norm_P_sq_le (P i) (u - sweepProd P l u)
    linarith

/-- Weighted comparison: for a duplicate-free list, `w_min ∑_{x ∈ l} fₓ ≤ ∑ₓ wₓ fₓ` when
`0 ≤ w_min ≤ wₓ` and `fₓ ≥ 0`. -/
theorem wmin_mul_listSum_le [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] (w f : ι → ℝ) {wmin : ℝ}
    (hwmin : 0 ≤ wmin) (hw : ∀ x, wmin ≤ w x) (hf : ∀ x, 0 ≤ f x) (l : List ι) (hl : l.Nodup) :
    wmin * (l.map f).sum ≤ ∑ x, w x * f x := by
  rw [← List.sum_toFinset f hl, Finset.mul_sum]
  calc ∑ x ∈ l.toFinset, wmin * f x ≤ ∑ x ∈ l.toFinset, w x * f x :=
        Finset.sum_le_sum fun x _ => mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right (hw x) (hf x)
    _ ≤ ∑ x, w x * f x :=
        Finset.sum_le_sum_of_subset_of_nonneg (Finset.subset_univ _)
          fun x _ _ => mul_nonneg (hwmin.trans (hw x)) (hf x)

/-- Several pairwise disjoint duplicate-free lists:
`w_min ∑_j ∑_{x ∈ L j} fₓ ≤ ∑ₓ wₓ fₓ`. -/
theorem wmin_mul_listsSum_le [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] {κ : Type*} [Fintype κ]
    (w f : ι → ℝ) {wmin : ℝ} (hwmin : 0 ≤ wmin) (hw : ∀ x, wmin ≤ w x) (hf : ∀ x, 0 ≤ f x)
    (L : κ → List ι) (hnd : ∀ j, (L j).Nodup)
    (hdisj : ∀ j j', j ≠ j' → ∀ x ∈ L j, x ∉ L j') :
    ∑ j, wmin * ((L j).map f).sum ≤ ∑ x, w x * f x := by
  classical
  have hpd : ((Finset.univ : Finset κ) : Set κ).PairwiseDisjoint fun j => (L j).toFinset := by
    intro j _ j' _ hjj'
    rw [Function.onFun, Finset.disjoint_left]
    intro x hx hx'
    exact hdisj j j' hjj' x (List.mem_toFinset.1 hx) (List.mem_toFinset.1 hx')
  calc ∑ j, wmin * ((L j).map f).sum = ∑ j, ∑ x ∈ (L j).toFinset, wmin * f x := by
        refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => ?_
        rw [← List.sum_toFinset f (hnd j), Finset.mul_sum]
    _ = ∑ x ∈ Finset.univ.biUnion (fun j => (L j).toFinset), wmin * f x :=
        (Finset.sum_biUnion hpd).symm
    _ ≤ ∑ x ∈ Finset.univ.biUnion (fun j => (L j).toFinset), w x * f x :=
        Finset.sum_le_sum fun x _ => mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right (hw x) (hf x)
    _ ≤ ∑ x, w x * f x :=
        Finset.sum_le_sum_of_subset_of_nonneg (Finset.subset_univ _)
          fun x _ _ => mul_nonneg (hwmin.trans (hw x)) (hf x)

/-- **`hcons` from contracting sweeps.** Let `P'ₓ` and `Π` be orthogonal projections, `0 ≤ w_min ≤ wₓ`,
and `L j` (`j : κ`, `m = card κ`) pairwise disjoint duplicate-free lists of indices. If every sweep
`Q_j = ∏_{x ∈ L j} P'ₓ` satisfies `‖Q_j u‖ ≤ θ ‖u‖` on `ker Π` with `θ ≤ 1`, then
`m · w_min · (1 − θ)² · ‖u‖² ≤ ∑ₓ wₓ ‖u − P'ₓ u‖²` on `ker Π` (the form of `hcons` in Part X). -/
theorem hcons_of_sweeps [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] {κ : Type*} [Fintype κ] (w : ι → ℝ)
    {wmin θ : ℝ} (hwmin : 0 ≤ wmin) (hw : ∀ x, wmin ≤ w x) (P' : ι → OrthProj H)
    (pj : OrthProj H) (L : κ → List ι) (hnd : ∀ j, (L j).Nodup)
    (hdisj : ∀ j j', j ≠ j' → ∀ x ∈ L j, x ∉ L j') (hθ1 : θ ≤ 1)
    (hsweep : ∀ j u, pj.P u = 0 → ‖sweepProd P' (L j) u‖ ≤ θ * ‖u‖) :
    ∀ u, pj.P u = 0 →
      ((Fintype.card κ : ℝ) * wmin * (1 - θ) ^ 2) * ‖u‖ ^ 2 ≤
        ∑ x, w x * ‖u - (P' x).P u‖ ^ 2 := by
  intro u hu
  have hj : ∀ j, wmin * ((1 - θ) ^ 2 * ‖u‖ ^ 2) ≤
      wmin * ((L j).map fun x => ‖u - (P' x).P u‖ ^ 2).sum := by
    intro j
    refine mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left ?_ hwmin
    have h1 : (1 - θ) * ‖u‖ ≤ ‖u - sweepProd P' (L j) u‖ := by
      have ht := norm_sub_norm_le u (sweepProd P' (L j) u)
      linarith [hsweep j u hu]
    have h0 : 0 ≤ (1 - θ) * ‖u‖ := mul_nonneg (by linarith) (norm_nonneg u)
    calc (1 - θ) ^ 2 * ‖u‖ ^ 2 = ((1 - θ) * ‖u‖) ^ 2 := by ring
      _ ≤ ‖u - sweepProd P' (L j) u‖ ^ 2 := pow_le_pow_left₀ h0 h1 2
      _ ≤ _ := norm_sub_sweepProd_sq_le P' u (L j)
  calc ((Fintype.card κ : ℝ) * wmin * (1 - θ) ^ 2) * ‖u‖ ^ 2 =
        ∑ _j : κ, wmin * ((1 - θ) ^ 2 * ‖u‖ ^ 2) := by
        rw [Finset.sum_const, Finset.card_univ, nsmul_eq_mul]; ring
    _ ≤ ∑ j, wmin * ((L j).map fun x => ‖u - (P' x).P u‖ ^ 2).sum :=
        Finset.sum_le_sum fun j _ => hj j
    _ ≤ ∑ x, w x * ‖u - (P' x).P u‖ ^ 2 :=
        wmin_mul_listsSum_le w (fun x => ‖u - (P' x).P u‖ ^ 2) hwmin hw (fun _ => sq_nonneg _)
          L hnd hdisj

/-- **`hcons` from one vanishing sweep** (the abstract form of the `β = 0` argument). If the
ordered product of the `P'ₓ` along one duplicate-free list vanishes on `ker Π`, then
`hcons` holds with `λ = w_min`. -/
theorem hcons_of_sweep_vanish [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] (w : ι → ℝ) {wmin : ℝ}
    (hwmin : 0 ≤ wmin) (hw : ∀ x, wmin ≤ w x) (P' : ι → OrthProj H) (pj : OrthProj H)
    (l : List ι) (hl : l.Nodup) (hvan : ∀ u, pj.P u = 0 → sweepProd P' l u = 0) :
    ∀ u, pj.P u = 0 → wmin * ‖u‖ ^ 2 ≤ ∑ x, w x * ‖u - (P' x).P u‖ ^ 2 := by
  intro u hu
  have h := hcons_of_sweeps (κ := Unit) w hwmin hw P' pj (fun _ => l) (fun _ => hl)
    (fun j j' hjj' => absurd (Subsingleton.elim j j') hjj') zero_le_one
    (fun _ v hv => by rw [hvan v hv, norm_zero, zero_mul]) u hu
  simpa using h

/-- `hFibre` from contracting sweeps of the constrained projections: `hcons_of_sweeps` fed into
`fibre_of_constrained` (Part X). -/
theorem fibre_of_sweeps [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] {κ : Type*} [Fintype κ] (w : ι → ℝ)
    {wmin θ : ℝ} (hwmin : 0 ≤ wmin) (hw : ∀ x, wmin ≤ w x) (P P' : ι → OrthProj H)
    (hle : ∀ x z, (P' x).P ((P x).P z) = (P x).P z) (pj : OrthProj H)
    (hcoarse : ∀ x z, (P' x).P (pj.P z) = pj.P z) (L : κ → List ι) (hnd : ∀ j, (L j).Nodup)
    (hdisj : ∀ j j', j ≠ j' → ∀ x ∈ L j, x ∉ L j') (hθ1 : θ ≤ 1)
    (hsweep : ∀ j u, pj.P u = 0 → ‖sweepProd P' (L j) u‖ ≤ θ * ‖u‖) :
    ∀ u, pj.P u = 0 → ((Fintype.card κ : ℝ) * wmin * (1 - θ) ^ 2) * ‖u‖ ^ 2 ≤
      ⟪u, cubeGen w (fun x => (P x).P) u⟫_ℝ :=
  (fibre_of_constrained w (fun x => hwmin.trans (hw x)) P P' hle pj hcoarse
    (hcons_of_sweeps w hwmin hw P' pj L hnd hdisj hθ1 hsweep)).2

/-! ### Commuting families: `I − ∏ P ≤ ∑ (I − P)` as forms -/

theorem sweepProd_commute (P : ι → OrthProj H) (hc : ∀ i j, Commute (P i).P (P j).P) (i : ι)
    (l : List ι) : Commute (P i).P (sweepProd P l) :=
  Commute.list_prod_right _ _ fun y hy => by
    obtain ⟨j, _, rfl⟩ := List.mem_map.1 hy
    exact hc i j

/-- For a pairwise commuting family the sweep product is idempotent and symmetric. -/
theorem sweepProd_isOrthProj (P : ι → OrthProj H) (hc : ∀ i j, Commute (P i).P (P j).P) :
    ∀ l : List ι, (∀ x, sweepProd P l (sweepProd P l x) = sweepProd P l x) ∧
      (sweepProd P l).IsSymmetric
  | [] => ⟨fun x => rfl, fun x y => rfl⟩
  | i :: l => by
    obtain ⟨hid, hsy⟩ := sweepProd_isOrthProj P hc l
    have hcom := sweepProd_commute P hc i l
    refine ⟨fun x => ?_, fun x y => ?_⟩
    · simp only [sweepProd_cons]
      have h1 : sweepProd P l ((P i).P (sweepProd P l x)) =
          (P i).P (sweepProd P l (sweepProd P l x)) := by
        have := congrArg (fun T : H →ₗ[ℝ] H => T (sweepProd P l x)) hcom.eq
        simpa [Module.End.mul_apply] using this.symm
      rw [h1, hid, (P i).idem]
    · simp only [sweepProd_cons]
      rw [(P i).symm, hsy]
      have h1 : (P i).P (sweepProd P l y) = sweepProd P l ((P i).P y) := by
        have := congrArg (fun T : H →ₗ[ℝ] H => T y) hcom.eq
        simpa [Module.End.mul_apply] using this
      rw [h1]

/-- The product of a pairwise commuting family along a list, as an orthogonal projection. -/
def sweepProj (P : ι → OrthProj H) (hc : ∀ i j, Commute (P i).P (P j).P) (l : List ι) :
    OrthProj H where
  P := sweepProd P l
  idem := (sweepProd_isOrthProj P hc l).1
  symm := (sweepProd_isOrthProj P hc l).2

/-- **`I − ∏ₓ Pₓ ≤ ∑ₓ (I − Pₓ)` as quadratic forms** for a pairwise commuting finite family of
orthogonal projections (product along any duplicate-free list of all indices, e.g.
`Finset.univ.toList`). -/
theorem form_sweepProj_le_cubeGen [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] (P : ι → OrthProj H)
    (hc : ∀ i j, Commute (P i).P (P j).P) (l : List ι) (hl : l.Nodup) (u : H) :
    ⟪u, u - (sweepProj P hc l).P u⟫_ℝ ≤ ⟪u, cubeGen (fun _ => (1 : ℝ)) (fun x => (P x).P) u⟫_ℝ := by
  rw [(sweepProj P hc l).inner_sub_P_self, inner_cubeGen_eq]
  have h1 := norm_sub_sweepProd_sq_le P u l
  have h2 := wmin_mul_listSum_le (fun _ => (1 : ℝ)) (fun x => ‖u - (P x).P u‖ ^ 2) zero_le_one
    (fun _ => le_rfl) (fun _ => sq_nonneg _) l hl
  rw [one_mul] at h2
  exact h1.trans h2

end Abstract

/-! ### The Wilson and SU(2) instances -/

section Wilson

variable {S E G : Type*} [OrientedGraph S E] [Fintype E] [Group G] [MeasurableSpace G]
  [MeasurableMul₂ G] [MeasurableInv G] {Pl : Type*} [Fintype Pl] (plaq : Pl → Plaq S E)
  (χ : ClassFn G) (h : MeasureTheory.Measure G) [MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure h]

omit [MeasurableMul₂ G] [MeasurableInv G] in
/-- **At `κ = 0` the Wilson measure is the product measure** `∏ₑ h`. -/
theorem wilsonMeasure_zero :
    wilsonMeasure plaq χ 0 h = MeasureTheory.Measure.pi fun _ : E => h := by
  have h0 : wilsonExp plaq χ 0 = fun _ => 0 := by
    funext U
    simp [wilsonExp]
  rw [wilsonMeasure, h0]
  exact MeasureTheory.tilted_zero _

end Wilson

section SU2

/-- The side-2 cube based at the source of a link contains that link. -/
theorem mem_cube2_self (M : ℕ) (x : Site (2 * M)) (μ : Fin 4) : (x, μ) ∈ cube2 M x :=
  ⟨fun _ => 0, rfl, by funext i; simp⟩

/-- **The constrained cubes cover every non-skeleton link**: `⋃ₓ (cube2 M x ∖ Sk) = Skᶜ`
(every `M`, straight blocking). This is step (iii) of the `β = 0` argument. -/
theorem iUnion_cube2_diff_skel (M : ℕ) :
    (⋃ x : Site (2 * M), cube2 M x \ skel (straightBlocking M)) = (skel (straightBlocking M))ᶜ := by
  ext e
  simp only [Set.mem_iUnion, Set.mem_sdiff, Set.mem_compl_iff]
  exact ⟨fun ⟨_, _, h⟩ => h, fun h => ⟨e.1, mem_cube2_self M e.1 e.2, h⟩⟩

variable (M : ℕ) [NeZero M] (β : ℝ)

/-- **`hFibre` for SU(2) on `(ℤ/2Mℤ)⁴` from contracting constrained sweeps.** For every `M ≥ 1`,
every real `β`, any link sets `Vₓ` and weights `wₓ ≥ w_min ≥ 0`: if `m` pairwise disjoint
duplicate-free lists of cubes have constrained sweeps `∏ P_{Vₓ ∖ Sk}` contracting by `θ ≤ 1`
on `ker Π`, then `hFibre` holds for `D = ∑ₓ wₓ (I − P_{Vₓ})` with `λ = m w_min (1 − θ)²`. -/
theorem su2_hFibre_of_sweeps {ι κ : Type*} [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] [Fintype κ]
    (V : ι → Set (Link (2 * M))) (w : ι → ℝ) {wmin θ : ℝ} (hwmin : 0 ≤ wmin)
    (hw : ∀ x, wmin ≤ w x) (L : κ → List ι) (hnd : ∀ j, (L j).Nodup)
    (hdisj : ∀ j j', j ≠ j' → ∀ x ∈ L j, x ∉ L j') (hθ1 : θ ≤ 1)
    (hsweep : ∀ j u, (su2Pi M β).P u = 0 →
      ‖sweepProd (fun x => wilsonPj (plaqOf (n := 2 * M)) reTr (β / 2) haarSU2
        (V x \ skel (straightBlocking M))) (L j) u‖ ≤ θ * ‖u‖) :
    ∀ u, (su2Pi M β).P u = 0 →
      ((Fintype.card κ : ℝ) * wmin * (1 - θ) ^ 2) * ‖u‖ ^ 2 ≤
        ⟪u, cubeGen w (fun x => su2P M β (V x)) u⟫_ℝ :=
  su2_hFibre_of_constrained M β V w (fun x => hwmin.trans (hw x))
    (hcons_of_sweeps w hwmin hw
      (fun x => wilsonPj (plaqOf (n := 2 * M)) reTr (β / 2) haarSU2
        (V x \ skel (straightBlocking M))) (su2Pi M β) L hnd hdisj hθ1 hsweep)

end SU2

end YangMills.StrongCoupling.ConstrainedFibre

/-! # Part XIV. `YangMills.StrongCoupling.SchurTower`: test-vector upper bounds on the split constants, "no compensation", and an obstruction instance (new; uses Parts I, II and IX) -/

/-!
# Upper bounds on the split constants of a tower, from test vectors

This part concerns **reversible heat-bath (cube-resampling) generators** `D_k` at scales
`k = 0, 1, 2, …`, composed by the splits of Part IX. It is not about transfer matrices and it is
**not a mass-gap statement**.

## (a) Formal target

Part IX (`gap_tower`, `gap_tower_closed`) turns splits `α_k (I − Π_k) + β_k J_k D_{k+1} J_k* ≤ D_k`
into a lower bound `towerBound` on `D_0`, and `towerBound_le_prod`, `gap_le_of_fixed` cap that bound by
`ϖ_K ∏ β` and `ϖ_K ≤ ∑_{x∈Z} wₓ`. This part bounds the `β_k` themselves from above by test vectors,
so that the cap becomes computable: it is the abstract half of an obstruction for straight blocking in
four dimensions at Gaussian order (the lattice half — the Gaussian infrared evaluation of the test
ratio, for split constants independent of the volume — is a paper proof and an exact rational
computation outside Lean, in the research notes).

## (b) What is proved

* `StepAt.test_upper`: at one scale, with `α_k ≥ 0`, for **every** `x` (not only `x = J y` as in
  `coarse_lower`): `β_k ⟪J* x, D_{k+1} J* x⟫ ≤ ⟪x, D_k x⟫`.
* `Jtcomp`, `tower_test_upper`, `tower_prod_le_ratio`: telescoped over `m` scales with the composed
  coarse-graining `𝒥* = J*_{k+m−1} ⋯ J*_k`: `(∏_{i<m} β_{k+i}) ⟪𝒥* x, D_{k+m} 𝒥* x⟫ ≤ ⟪x, D_k x⟫`, so
  `∏ β ≤ ⟪x, D_k x⟫ / ⟪𝒥* x, D_{k+m} 𝒥* x⟫` for every test vector with positive denominator. Only the
  bottom and the top generator enter; the intermediate ones cancel.
* `tower_conclusion_le`: if the top generator is a cube generator `∑_z w_z (I − P_z)` with
  `ϖ ≤ D_{k+m}`, and `f ≠ 0` is fixed by `P_z` for `z ∉ Z`, then
  `towerBound ≤ (∑_{z∈Z} w_z) · ⟪x, D_k x⟫ / ⟪𝒥* x, D_{k+m} 𝒥* x⟫` for every test vector `x`: an
  explicit limit on what any such tower can conclude, whatever the `α`s ≥ 0, `ϖ` and intermediate
  designs.
* `towerBound_le_alpha_prod` ("no compensation"): `towerBound m k ≤ α_{k+j} ∏_{i<j} β_{k+i}` for every
  `j < m`; with `StepAt.alpha_form`, `StepAt.alpha_le_of_fixed` (a cap on `α_k` from a local vector),
  scales after `j` cannot undo a small prefix product `∏_{i<j} β`.
* `towerBound_le_pow`: the abstract per-scale obstruction — if `0 ≤ β_{k+i} ≤ θ/4` for `i < m` and
  `ϖ ≥ 0`, then `towerBound m k ≤ ϖ (θ/4)^m`.
* Non-vacuity (toy towers on `ℝ`, not the Wilson model): `example_doubling_step` (`D_k = 8ᵏ`,
  `α_k = 8ᵏ`, `β = 1/8`), `example_beta_le_eighth` (for that tower, every admissible `β_k ≤ 1/8`: an
  obstruction instance obtained from `StepAt.test_upper`), `example_doubling_tower`,
  `example_doubling_tower_value` (the bound `ϖ (1/8)³` is attained at `ϖ = 8³`).

## (c) What remains open

The identification of the test ratio for the Wilson model: at Gaussian order the research notes evaluate
`⟪x, D_0 x⟫ / ⟪𝒥* x, D_K 𝒥* x⟫` on smooth transverse plane waves (infrared limit) and bound it by
exact rational test fields; that evaluation, the Gaussian conditional-variance formulas and the
identification of the matrices with the lattice objects are not formalised here. Nothing is proved
about the interacting (non-Gaussian) blocked laws.

## (d) Axioms and checks

Every declaration depends only on `propext`, `Classical.choice` and `Quot.sound`; there is no
`sorry`, `admit`, `axiom`, `native_decide`, `implemented_by` or `set_option`. The module axiom
audit covers every headline theorem.

## (e) Scope

This part is not a proof of a mass gap, of a transfer-matrix gap, or of any statement about the
continuum. It bounds from above what the heat-bath Schur tower of Part IX can deliver.
-/

namespace YangMills.StrongCoupling.SchurTower

open scoped InnerProductSpace

section TestUpper

variable {H : ℕ → Type*} [∀ k, NormedAddCommGroup (H k)] [∀ k, InnerProductSpace ℝ (H k)]
  {D : ∀ k, H k →ₗ[ℝ] H k} {pj : ∀ k, SchurSplit.OrthProj (H k)}
  {J : ∀ k, H (k + 1) →ₗ[ℝ] H k} {Jt : ∀ k, H k →ₗ[ℝ] H (k + 1)} {α β : ℕ → ℝ}

/-- The composed coarse-graining `J*_{k+m−1} ⋯ J*_k : H k → H (k+m)`, as a function. -/
def Jtcomp (Jt : ∀ k, H k →ₗ[ℝ] H (k + 1)) (k : ℕ) : ∀ m, H k → H (k + m)
  | 0 => fun x => x
  | m + 1 => fun x => Jt (k + m) (Jtcomp Jt k m x)

/-- **Test-vector bound at one scale.** With `α_k ≥ 0`, the split gives
`β_k ⟪J* x, D_{k+1} J* x⟫ ≤ ⟪x, D_k x⟫` for every `x` (`coarse_lower` is the case `x = J y`). -/
theorem StepAt.test_upper {k : ℕ} (hs : StepAt D pj J Jt α β k) (hα : 0 ≤ α k) (x : H k) :
    β k * ⟪Jt k x, D (k + 1) (Jt k x)⟫_ℝ ≤ ⟪x, D k x⟫_ℝ := by
  have h := hs.form x
  have h0 : 0 ≤ α k * ‖x - (pj k).P x‖ ^ 2 := mul_nonneg hα (sq_nonneg _)
  linarith

/-- **Telescoped test-vector bound.** Splits at the scales `k, …, k+m−1` with `α, β ≥ 0` give
`(∏_{i<m} β_{k+i}) ⟪𝒥* x, D_{k+m} 𝒥* x⟫ ≤ ⟪x, D_k x⟫` for every `x`. -/
theorem tower_test_upper (k : ℕ) :
    ∀ m, (∀ i < m, 0 ≤ α (k + i)) → (∀ i < m, 0 ≤ β (k + i)) →
      (∀ i < m, StepAt D pj J Jt α β (k + i)) → ∀ x : H k,
        (∏ i ∈ Finset.range m, β (k + i)) *
          ⟪Jtcomp Jt k m x, D (k + m) (Jtcomp Jt k m x)⟫_ℝ ≤ ⟪x, D k x⟫_ℝ := by
  intro m
  induction m with
  | zero => intro _ _ _ x; simp [Jtcomp]
  | succ m ih =>
    intro hα hβ hs x
    have h1 := ih (fun i hi => hα i (by omega)) (fun i hi => hβ i (by omega))
      (fun i hi => hs i (by omega)) x
    have h2 := (hs m (by omega)).test_upper (hα m (by omega)) (Jtcomp Jt k m x)
    have hp : 0 ≤ ∏ i ∈ Finset.range m, β (k + i) :=
      Finset.prod_nonneg fun i hi => hβ i (by have := Finset.mem_range.1 hi; omega)
    have h3 := mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left h2 hp
    rw [Finset.prod_range_succ]
    show (∏ i ∈ Finset.range m, β (k + i)) * β (k + m) *
        ⟪Jt (k + m) (Jtcomp Jt k m x), D (k + m + 1) (Jt (k + m) (Jtcomp Jt k m x))⟫_ℝ ≤
      ⟪x, D k x⟫_ℝ
    rw [mul_assoc]
    linarith

/-- **The product of the split constants is at most a test ratio.** -/
theorem tower_prod_le_ratio (k m : ℕ) (hα : ∀ i < m, 0 ≤ α (k + i))
    (hβ : ∀ i < m, 0 ≤ β (k + i)) (hs : ∀ i < m, StepAt D pj J Jt α β (k + i)) (x : H k)
    (hpos : 0 < ⟪Jtcomp Jt k m x, D (k + m) (Jtcomp Jt k m x)⟫_ℝ) :
    ∏ i ∈ Finset.range m, β (k + i) ≤
      ⟪x, D k x⟫_ℝ / ⟪Jtcomp Jt k m x, D (k + m) (Jtcomp Jt k m x)⟫_ℝ := by
  rw [le_div_iff₀ hpos]
  exact tower_test_upper k m hα hβ hs x

/-- **What a tower can conclude, explicitly.** If the top generator is a cube generator
`∑_z w_z (I − P_z)` (orthogonal projections, `w ≥ 0`) with `ϖ • I ≤ D_{k+m}`, and `f ≠ 0` is fixed
by every `P_z` with `z ∉ Z`, then for every test vector `x`:
`towerBound m k ≤ (∑_{z∈Z} w_z) · ⟪x, D_k x⟫ / ⟪𝒥* x, D_{k+m} 𝒥* x⟫`. -/
theorem tower_conclusion_le {ϖ : ℝ} (k m : ℕ) {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] (w : ι → ℝ)
    (P : ι → H (k + m) →ₗ[ℝ] H (k + m)) (hw : ∀ z, 0 ≤ w z) (hPs : ∀ z, (P z).IsSymmetric)
    (hPi : ∀ z y, P z (P z y) = P z y) (Z : Finset ι) {f : H (k + m)} (hf : f ≠ 0)
    (hfix : ∀ z ∉ Z, P z f = f) (htop : ϖ • LinearMap.id ≤ D (k + m))
    (hD : D (k + m) = CubeSplit.cubeGen w P) (hα : ∀ i < m, 0 ≤ α (k + i))
    (hβ : ∀ i < m, 0 ≤ β (k + i)) (hs : ∀ i < m, StepAt D pj J Jt α β (k + i)) (x : H k)
    (hpos : 0 < ⟪Jtcomp Jt k m x, D (k + m) (Jtcomp Jt k m x)⟫_ℝ) :
    towerBound α β ϖ m k ≤ (∑ z ∈ Z, w z) *
      (⟪x, D k x⟫_ℝ / ⟪Jtcomp Jt k m x, D (k + m) (Jtcomp Jt k m x)⟫_ℝ) := by
  have h1 := towerBound_le_prod (α := α) (ϖ := ϖ) m k hβ
  have htop' : ϖ • LinearMap.id ≤ CubeSplit.cubeGen w P := by rw [← hD]; exact htop
  have hϖ : ϖ ≤ ∑ z ∈ Z, w z := gap_le_of_fixed w P hw hPs hPi Z hf hfix htop'
  have hprod := tower_prod_le_ratio k m hα hβ hs x hpos
  have hp0 : 0 ≤ ∏ i ∈ Finset.range m, β (k + i) :=
    Finset.prod_nonneg fun i hi => hβ i (Finset.mem_range.1 hi)
  have hW : 0 ≤ ∑ z ∈ Z, w z := Finset.sum_nonneg fun z _ => hw z
  calc towerBound α β ϖ m k ≤ ϖ * ∏ i ∈ Finset.range m, β (k + i) := h1
    _ ≤ (∑ z ∈ Z, w z) * ∏ i ∈ Finset.range m, β (k + i) := mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right hϖ hp0
    _ ≤ (∑ z ∈ Z, w z) *
        (⟪x, D k x⟫_ℝ / ⟪Jtcomp Jt k m x, D (k + m) (Jtcomp Jt k m x)⟫_ℝ) :=
      mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left hprod hW

/-- The split controls `α_k` by the generator alone (for `β_k ≥ 0` and `D_{k+1} ≥ 0` as a form):
`α_k ‖x − Π_k x‖² ≤ ⟪x, D_k x⟫`. -/
theorem StepAt.alpha_form {k : ℕ} (hs : StepAt D pj J Jt α β k) (hβ : 0 ≤ β k)
    (hDc : ∀ y, 0 ≤ ⟪y, D (k + 1) y⟫_ℝ) (x : H k) :
    α k * ‖x - (pj k).P x‖ ^ 2 ≤ ⟪x, D k x⟫_ℝ := by
  have h := hs.form x
  have h0 := mul_nonneg hβ (hDc (Jt k x))
  linarith

/-- **A cap on `α_k` from a local vector.** If `D_k = ∑_z w_z (I − P_z)` (orthogonal projections,
`w ≥ 0`) and `x` is fixed by every `P_z` with `z ∉ Z`, then
`α_k ‖x − Π_k x‖² ≤ (∑_{z∈Z} w_z) ‖x‖²`. -/
theorem StepAt.alpha_le_of_fixed {k : ℕ} (hs : StepAt D pj J Jt α β k) (hβ : 0 ≤ β k)
    (hDc : ∀ y, 0 ≤ ⟪y, D (k + 1) y⟫_ℝ) {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] (w : ι → ℝ)
    (P : ι → H k →ₗ[ℝ] H k) (hw : ∀ z, 0 ≤ w z) (hPs : ∀ z, (P z).IsSymmetric)
    (hPi : ∀ z y, P z (P z y) = P z y) (hD : D k = CubeSplit.cubeGen w P) (Z : Finset ι) (x : H k)
    (hfix : ∀ z ∉ Z, P z x = x) :
    α k * ‖x - (pj k).P x‖ ^ 2 ≤ (∑ z ∈ Z, w z) * ‖x‖ ^ 2 := by
  have h1 := hs.alpha_form hβ hDc x
  have h2 := form_le_of_fixed w P hw hPs hPi Z x hfix
  rw [← hD] at h2
  linarith

/-- **No compensation by later scales.** For `β ≥ 0` and every `j < m`:
`towerBound m k ≤ α_{k+j} ∏_{i<j} β_{k+i}`. -/
theorem towerBound_le_alpha_prod {ϖ : ℝ} :
    ∀ (m k : ℕ), (∀ i < m, 0 ≤ β (k + i)) → ∀ j < m,
      towerBound α β ϖ m k ≤ α (k + j) * ∏ i ∈ Finset.range j, β (k + i) := by
  intro m
  induction m with
  | zero => intro k _ j hj; exact absurd hj (Nat.not_lt_zero j)
  | succ m ih =>
    intro k hβ j hj
    have hβk : 0 ≤ β k := by simpa using hβ 0 (by omega)
    rcases j with _ | j
    · show min (α k) (β k * towerBound α β ϖ m (k + 1)) ≤
        α (k + 0) * ∏ i ∈ Finset.range 0, β (k + i)
      simp only [add_zero, Finset.prod_range_zero, mul_one]
      exact min_le_left _ _
    · have hβ' : ∀ i < m, 0 ≤ β (k + 1 + i) := fun i hi => by
        rw [show k + 1 + i = k + (i + 1) by omega]; exact hβ (i + 1) (by omega)
      have h1 := ih (k + 1) hβ' j (by omega)
      have h2 : towerBound α β ϖ (m + 1) k ≤ β k * towerBound α β ϖ m (k + 1) :=
        min_le_right _ _
      have h3 := mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left h1 hβk
      rw [prod_shift, show k + (j + 1) = k + 1 + j by omega]
      calc towerBound α β ϖ (m + 1) k ≤ β k * towerBound α β ϖ m (k + 1) := h2
        _ ≤ β k * (α (k + 1 + j) * ∏ i ∈ Finset.range j, β (k + 1 + i)) := h3
        _ = α (k + 1 + j) * (β k * ∏ i ∈ Finset.range j, β (k + 1 + i)) := by ring

/-- **The abstract per-scale obstruction.** If `0 ≤ β_{k+i} ≤ θ/4` for `i < m` and `ϖ ≥ 0`, then
`towerBound m k ≤ ϖ (θ/4)^m`. -/
theorem towerBound_le_pow {ϖ θ : ℝ} (hϖ : 0 ≤ ϖ) (m k : ℕ) (hβ0 : ∀ i < m, 0 ≤ β (k + i))
    (hβ : ∀ i < m, β (k + i) ≤ θ / 4) : towerBound α β ϖ m k ≤ ϖ * (θ / 4) ^ m := by
  have h1 := towerBound_le_prod (α := α) (ϖ := ϖ) m k hβ0
  have h2 : ∏ i ∈ Finset.range m, β (k + i) ≤ ∏ _i ∈ Finset.range m, (θ / 4) :=
    Finset.prod_le_prod (fun i hi => hβ0 i (Finset.mem_range.1 hi))
      (fun i hi => hβ i (Finset.mem_range.1 hi))
  rw [Finset.prod_const, Finset.card_range] at h2
  exact h1.trans (mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left h2 hϖ)

end TestUpper

/-! ## Non-vacuity (toy towers on `ℝ`, not the Wilson model) -/

section ScaleRatioExamples

/-- The "doubling" toy tower: `H k = ℝ`, `D_k = 8ᵏ` (diffusive `4ᵏ` times a per-scale speed-up `2ᵏ`,
the shape of the 4D Gaussian infrared constants `c_k ∝ 2ᵏ`), `Π_k = J_k = I`, `α_k = 8ᵏ`,
`β_k = 1/8`. -/
theorem example_doubling_step (k : ℕ) :
    StepAt (H := fun _ => ℝ) (fun k => SchurSplit.scal ((8 : ℝ) ^ k)) (fun _ => pjId)
      (fun _ => LinearMap.id) (fun _ => LinearMap.id) (fun k => (8 : ℝ) ^ k) (fun _ => 1 / 8) k where
  symm := SchurSplit.scal_isSymmetric _
  adj _ _ := rfl
  JJt _ := rfl
  le := by
    show pjId.splitOp LinearMap.id LinearMap.id (SchurSplit.scal ((8 : ℝ) ^ (k + 1))) ((8 : ℝ) ^ k)
      (1 / 8) ≤ SchurSplit.scal ((8 : ℝ) ^ k)
    rw [pjId.splitOp_le_iff (SchurSplit.scal_isSymmetric _) (fun _ _ => rfl)
      (SchurSplit.scal_isSymmetric _)]
    intro x
    show (8 : ℝ) ^ k * ‖x - x‖ ^ 2 + 1 / 8 * ⟪x, SchurSplit.scal ((8 : ℝ) ^ (k + 1)) x⟫_ℝ ≤
      ⟪x, SchurSplit.scal ((8 : ℝ) ^ k) x⟫_ℝ
    rw [sub_self, norm_zero, SchurSplit.scal_apply, SchurSplit.scal_apply, SchurSplit.inner_real,
      SchurSplit.inner_real]
    apply le_of_eq
    ring

/-- **An obstruction instance.** For the doubling toy tower, every split constant allowed at scale
`k` (with `α_k ≥ 0`) satisfies `β_k ≤ 1/8`, i.e. `4 β_k ≤ 1/2`: `StepAt.test_upper` at `x = 1`. -/
theorem example_beta_le_eighth (α β : ℕ → ℝ) (k : ℕ) (hα : 0 ≤ α k)
    (hs : StepAt (H := fun _ => ℝ) (fun k => SchurSplit.scal ((8 : ℝ) ^ k)) (fun _ => pjId)
      (fun _ => LinearMap.id) (fun _ => LinearMap.id) α β k) : β k ≤ 1 / 8 := by
  have h := hs.test_upper hα (1 : ℝ)
  have e1 : ⟪(LinearMap.id : ℝ →ₗ[ℝ] ℝ) 1, SchurSplit.scal ((8 : ℝ) ^ (k + 1))
      ((LinearMap.id : ℝ →ₗ[ℝ] ℝ) 1)⟫_ℝ = (8 : ℝ) ^ k * 8 := by
    rw [LinearMap.id_apply, SchurSplit.scal_apply, SchurSplit.inner_real, pow_succ]; ring
  have e2 : ⟪(1 : ℝ), SchurSplit.scal ((8 : ℝ) ^ k) 1⟫_ℝ = (8 : ℝ) ^ k := by
    rw [SchurSplit.scal_apply, SchurSplit.inner_real]; ring
  change β k * ⟪(LinearMap.id : ℝ →ₗ[ℝ] ℝ) 1, SchurSplit.scal ((8 : ℝ) ^ (k + 1))
      ((LinearMap.id : ℝ →ₗ[ℝ] ℝ) 1)⟫_ℝ ≤ ⟪(1 : ℝ), SchurSplit.scal ((8 : ℝ) ^ k) 1⟫_ℝ at h
  rw [e1, e2] at h
  have hp : (0 : ℝ) < 8 ^ k := by positivity
  by_contra hc
  have h4 := mul_lt_mul_of_pos_left (not_le.mp hc) hp
  nlinarith

/-- The tower bound of the doubling toy tower over `m` scales is at most `ϖ (1/8)^m`
(`towerBound_le_pow` with `θ = 1/2`). -/
theorem example_doubling_tower (ϖ : ℝ) (hϖ : 0 ≤ ϖ) (m : ℕ) :
    towerBound (fun k => (8 : ℝ) ^ k) (fun _ => (1 / 8 : ℝ)) ϖ m 0 ≤ ϖ * ((1 / 2 : ℝ) / 4) ^ m :=
  towerBound_le_pow hϖ m 0 (fun _ _ => by norm_num) (fun _ _ => by norm_num)

/-- The bound is attained: with `α_k = 8ᵏ`, `β = 1/8` and `ϖ = 8³`, the three-scale tower bound is
exactly `1 = ϖ (1/8)³` (and `D_0 = 1`). -/
theorem example_doubling_tower_value :
    towerBound (fun k => (8 : ℝ) ^ k) (fun _ => (1 / 8 : ℝ)) ((8 : ℝ) ^ 3) 3 0 = 1 := by
  show min ((8 : ℝ) ^ 0) (1 / 8 * min ((8 : ℝ) ^ (0 + 1)) (1 / 8 * min ((8 : ℝ) ^ (0 + 1 + 1))
    (1 / 8 * (8 : ℝ) ^ 3))) = 1
  norm_num

end ScaleRatioExamples

end YangMills.StrongCoupling.SchurTower

/-! # Part XV. `YangMills.StrongCoupling.ProductEndpoint`: the interface inputs at the strong-coupling endpoint `β = 0` (new; uses Parts I–IV, VI, VII, IX, X and XII) -/

/-!
# The interface inputs at the strong-coupling endpoint `β = 0`

## (a) Formal target

At `κ = 0` (for SU(2), `κ = β/2` and `β = 0`) the Wilson measure of Part IV is the product measure
`∏ₑ h` (Part XII, `wilsonMeasure_zero`). The target is to verify, for the actual operators of
Parts III, IV, VI and X (`wilsonP`, `wilsonJ`, `isoProj`, `coarseLaw`, `coarseP`, `su2D`, `su2Dc`), the
inputs of `CubeSplitInputs.gap_of_residual` (Part II) at this endpoint: `hFibre`, `hCoarseGap` and
`hResidual`, together with the product-measure facts they rest on.

## (b) What is proved

* Product measures, abstract (`condExp_sup_indep_eq`, `condL2_extSigma_comp`,
  `condL2_extSigma_commute`): conditioning on a σ-algebra independent of the data changes nothing;
  hence for any measure equal to a product of probability measures on `E → G` the exterior
  conditional expectations compose, `E[E[f | ext W] | ext V] = E[f | ext (V ∪ W)]` in `L²`, and
  commute.
* Cube projections of a product measure on the centred gauge-invariant space (`extProj`,
  `extProj_comp`, `extProj_empty`, `extProj_univ`, `sweepProd_extProj`, `extProj_gap_of_cover`):
  `P_V P_W = P_{V ∪ W}`, `P_∅ = I`, `P_E = 0`, the sweep of Part XII along a list is `P` of the union,
  and a family covering every link with `wₓ ≥ w_min ≥ 0` gives `w_min ‖u‖² ≤ ⟪u, ∑ₓ wₓ (I − Pₓ) u⟫`.
* The Wilson model at `κ = 0` (`wilsonP_comp_zero`, `wilsonP_commute_zero`, `wilson_sweepProd_zero`,
  `wilson_gap_zero`), any finite oriented lattice, any group with a bi-invariant probability measure `h`.
* The blocked law at `κ = 0` (`map_comp_pi`, `measurePreserving_mul_pi`, `map_blockMap_pi`,
  `coarseLaw_eq_pi`, `coarse_gap_zero`): if the fine links `a ē`, `b ē` of the coarse links are pairwise
  distinct, `c_* (∏ₑ h) = ∏_ē h`, and a covering coarse family with weights `≥ ϖ ≥ 0` gives
  `ϖ • I ≤ D_c` (`hCoarseGap`). `straightBlocking_sumElim_injective`: straight blocking qualifies.
* Shears (`shear`, `measurePreserving_shear`, `measurable_shear_extSigma`, `condExp_comp_eq`): the map
  `U(t ē) ↦ φ(U(t ē), U(p ē))` preserves the product measure when each `φ(·, y)` does, and conditional
  expectation is transported along it.
* The mixed block at `κ = 0` (`condExp_comp_aestronglyMeasurable_comap`, `exists_coarseJ_eq`,
  `wilsonP_wilsonJ_mem_range`, `wilsonP_mem_ranPi`, `wilson_blkB_zero`): for a blocking whose fine
  links `a ē`, `b ē` are pairwise distinct, every cube projection maps `ran J = ran Π` into itself,
  for every link set, so `B = (I − Π) D Π = 0` for every cube family.
* SU(2) on `(ℤ/2Mℤ)⁴`, `β = 0`, every `M ≥ 1`, side-2 cubes `cube2 M x` at every base point with weights
  `1/16`, straight blocking, side-2 coarse cubes `sideTwoCube M z` at every coarse base point with
  weights `1/16`: `su2_fine_gap_zero` (`D ≥ (1/16) I` on `H`), `su2_hFibre_zero` (`hFibre`, `λ = 1/16`),
  `su2_coarseLaw_zero`, `su2_coarse_gap_zero` (`hCoarseGap`, `ϖ_c = 1/16`), `su2_sweep_cube2_zero`,
  `su2_blkB_zero`, `su2_hResidual_zero` (`hResidual` with `X = 0`, `β' = M⁻⁴`), and
  `su2_gap_closed_zero`: `CubeSplitInputs.gap_of_residual` for `su2_inputs` with
  every input proved (`hResidual` with `X = 0` and `β' = M⁻⁴`), giving `D ≥ min(α, M⁻⁴/16) I` for
  every `α < 1/16`. `hResidual_zero_of_blkB`, `gap_of_blkB_zero` and `inner_cubeGen_le_sum` are the
  general Hilbert-space steps used for it (compare `SmallCoupling.blkB_eq_zero_of_invariant` and
  `SmallCoupling.gap_of_invariant`, which assume that every cube projection preserves `ran Π` and
  `β' G ≤ C` on `H_c`, instead of `B = 0`, `D ≥ w_min` and `D_c ≤ c_D`).

## (c) What remains open

At `β = 0` the heat-bath gap of a product measure is elementary, and `su2_gap_closed_zero` is weaker
than `su2_fine_gap_zero`; the content is that the actual Wilson operators of Parts IV, VI and X meet
the interface inputs of Part II, which is kernel-checked here at this one coupling. The identity
`E_μ[· | σ(skeleton)] = Π` on `H` (Lemma IV of the accompanying research notes) is not formalised,
so the constrained bound `hcons` of Part X and `su2_gap_of_constrained` are not discharged here;
`hFibre` is obtained directly from the generator bound instead. The coarse comparison constant
`β' = M⁻⁴` depends on the volume. Nothing here concerns `β ≠ 0`, uniformity in the spacing,
infinite volume or a continuum limit.

## (d) Axioms and checks

Every headline depends only on `propext`, `Classical.choice` and `Quot.sound` (the module axiom
audit covers every headline theorem); the part contains no `sorry`, `admit`, `axiom` declarations,
`native_decide`, `implemented_by` or `set_option`.

## (e) Scope

This part is not a proof of a mass gap. Its statements about the Wilson model are finite-volume
statements at the single coupling `κ = 0` (`β = 0` for SU(2)), where the Wilson measure is a product
measure and the heat-bath gap is elementary; its other lemmas are general facts about product
measures, conditional expectations and the interface of Part II. Nothing here concerns `β ≠ 0`.
-/

