/-! # Part XVI. `YangMills.StrongCoupling.SmallCoupling`: the residual and coarse-gap inputs with the zero trial operator, and assembly lemmas for small coupling (new; uses Parts I–IV, VI, IX and X) -/

/-!
# Small coupling: the residual and coarse-gap inputs of the cube split with the zero trial operator

## (a) Formal target

`CubeSplitInputs.gap_of_residual` (Part II of this file) and `su2_gap_of_constrained` (Part X) turn
four inputs into the bound `D ≥ min(α, β' ϖ_c) I` for the cube generator `D = ∑ₓ wₓ (I − Pₓ)`:
`hWilson`, `hFibre` (or the constrained bound `hcons`), `hResidual` and `hCoarseGap`. The target here
is the abstract interface for the strong-coupling regime: `hResidual` with the zero trial operator
`X = 0` from *local* bounds (a bound on the mixed block `B = (I − Π) D Π` and a comparison of the
coarse form with `C = Π D Π`, both measured by one nonnegative functional `Γ` on `H_c`), and
`hCoarseGap` and `hcons` from single-site Poincaré inequalities through covers by cubes.

## (b) What is proved

* `qForm_zero_trial`, `resid_zero_trial`: for `X = 0`, `Q = 0` and `R = B`.
* `cert_zero_of_local`: if `‖B v‖² ≤ ε_B Γ v`, `⟪J* v, D_c J* v⟫ ≤ K_g Γ v`, `c Γ v ≤ ⟪v, C v⟫`,
  `Γ ≥ 0`, `β' ≥ 0` and `β' K_g + ε_B / (λ − α) ≤ c`, then the certificate of
  `split_of_certificate` holds with `X = 0`. No operator norm of `D` enters.
* `blkB_eq_zero_of_invariant`, `gap_of_invariant`: if every cube projection maps `ran Π` into
  itself, the mixed block vanishes, and `β' G ≤ C` on `H_c` is then the whole residual input.
* `gap_of_local_residual`: `gap_of_residual` with `X = 0` and the local bounds.
* `norm_sub_P_le_of_fix` (best approximation), `norm_sub_le_of_lift` (an isometry `J` that maps
  `ran Q` into `ran P` gives `‖J y − P J y‖ ≤ ‖y − Q y‖`), `poinc_of_lift` (a Poincaré inequality for
  single-site projections on `ran J` gives one for coarse projections, with a multiplicity factor).
* `sum_ge_of_cover`, `cubeGen_gap_of_cover`: if `ran Pₓ ⊆ ran Q_j` for the `≤ N` indices `j ∈ sₓ` and
  every `j` is covered with weight `≥ m`, then `∑ₓ wₓ ‖u − Pₓ u‖² ≥ (m / N) ∑_j ‖u − Q_j u‖²`; with a
  Poincaré inequality for the `Q_j` this is a gap of the cube generator.
* `gap_of_covers`: the assembly. `hWilson`, a Poincaré inequality on `ker Π` for fine single-site
  projections covering the constrained cubes, a Poincaré inequality for coarse single-site
  projections covering the coarse cubes, and the local residual bounds give
  `D ≥ min(α, β' (m_c / N_c) c_c) I` with `α < (m_f / N_f) c_f`.
* `gap_of_dobrushin_inputs`: the same assembly with the fibre bound supplied by `fibre_of_dobrushin`
  of Part X for the constrained cube projections themselves and the coarse Poincaré inequality by
  `dobrushin_gap` of Part X for single-site coarse projections (no Wilson instance of its Dobrushin
  hypotheses is known).
* SU(2) on `(ℤ/2Mℤ)⁴`, every `M ≥ 1`, every real `β`: `su2CoarsePj` (the coarse cube projection as
  an orthogonal projection), `su2_gap_of_local_residual` (`su2_gap_of_constrained` with `X = 0` and
  the local bounds) and `su2_gap_of_covers` (`hcons` and `hCoarseGap` from covers).

## (c) What remains open

All Wilson-specific estimates are hypotheses here: the mixed-block bound `‖B v‖² ≤ ε_B Γ v`, the
coarse comparison `G ≤ K_g Γ`, the lower bound `C ≥ c Γ`, the fibre Poincaré inequality on `ker Π`
and the single-link Poincaré inequality behind the coarse gap. The accompanying research notes give
paper proofs of these for SU(2), `d = 4`, straight blocking, side-2 cubes at every base point and
weights `1/16`, for `|β| < 1/72` and every `M ≥ 1`, with constants independent of `M`; with
`X = 0`, `λ = (1 − 72|β|)/56` and `α = λ/2` the budget `hbud` then closes for `|β| ≤ 1/1000`.
These proofs are not formalised. The Dobrushin hypotheses of `gap_of_dobrushin_inputs` (real-valued
seminorms on the whole of `ker Π` and of the coarse space) are not verified for the Wilson model.
At weak coupling `hcons`, `hResidual` and `hCoarseGap` remain open (`hWilson` is `su2_inputs` of
Part VI for every `β`).

## (d) Axioms and checks

Every headline depends only on `propext`, `Classical.choice` and `Quot.sound` (module axiom
audit), and the part contains no unfinished-proof markers, no new axiom declarations, no native
evaluation and no `set_option`. It uses Parts I, II, III, IV, VI, IX and X of this file.

## (e) Scope

This is not a proof of a mass gap. Heat-bath gaps at strong coupling are classical; the direct
single-link Dobrushin bound of the accompanying notes gives `D ≥ (1 − 72|β|)/64` on the same space
for `|β| < 1/72`, more than the split route returns. The Lean statements of this part are
implications whose Wilson-specific inputs are hypotheses; that these inputs hold at strong
coupling is a paper argument, a consistency check of the interface of the split route, not new
physics. The SU(2) statements are in finite volume. It says nothing about weak coupling or a
continuum limit.
-/

