/-! # Part XXVII. `YangMills.StrongCoupling.FibreNonVacuity`: `ker Π ≠ 0` for SU(2) straight blocking, so the statements on `ker Π` in Parts X, XII, XVII, XXI and XXII are not vacuous (new; uses Parts II–IV, VI, X, XII, XVII and XXI) -/

/-!
# Non-vacuity of the fibre statements: `ker Π ≠ 0` for SU(2) on `(ℤ/2Mℤ)⁴`

## (a) Formal target

For the SU(2) Wilson measure `μ ∝ exp((β/2) ∑ₚ Re tr U_p) ∏ₑ dUₑ` on `(ℤ/2Mℤ)⁴` (Part VI's
`su2Wilson`, so `β = β_W = 4/g²`) with the straight two-link blocking, show that the fibre space
`H_f = ker Π ⊆ H` (centred gauge-invariant `L²(μ)`, `Π = J J*`) contains a nonzero vector for every
`M ≥ 1` and every real `β`. Then the statements of Parts X, XII, XVII, XXI that assume `Π u = 0`
concern a nonzero space and are not vacuous.

## (b) What is proved

* `su2Pi_plaqH_ne`, `su2_kerPi_ne_zero` (every `M ≥ 1`, every real `β`): for `F = Re tr U_p` at the
  plaquette `q0` and `F̃ = F − μ(F) ∈ H`, `Π F̃ ≠ F̃`, so `u = F̃ − Π F̃` satisfies `Π u = 0`,
  `u ≠ 0`. Proof: by Lemma IV (Part XVII's `su2_skel_eq_Pi`), `Π = E_μ[· | σ(Sk)]` on `H`. If
  `Π F̃ = F̃`, then `F − μ(F) = g` `μ`-a.e. for a function `g` measurable for the σ-algebra of the
  skeleton links. The second link `(e₀, 1)` of `q0` is not a skeleton link (`q0_l2_not_mem_skel`).
  Left multiplication by `−I` on that link alone (`negAt`) preserves the product Haar measure
  (`measurePreserving_negAt`), leaves `g` unchanged pointwise (Part XVII's
  `eq_of_extSigma_measurable`) and maps `F` to `−F` (`plaqObs_negAt`). Since the product Haar
  measure is absolutely continuous with respect to `μ`, `F = 0` almost everywhere for it; but `F`
  is continuous and takes the values `2` and `−2` (Part VI's `not_ae_const_pi`). No continuity of
  `g` is used.
* `su2_skelKer_ne_zero`, `su2_Hf_ne_bot`: the same vector in the form `E_μ[u | σ(Sk)] = 0`, `u ≠ 0`
  (the domain condition of Part XXI's `SU2HeatBathInfluence`); `H_f ≠ 0` and `Π ≠ I`.
* `exists_pos_of_ker_bound`: any bound `λ ‖u‖² ≤ Q u` on `ker Π` with `λ > 0` gives `Q u > 0` for
  a nonzero `u ∈ ker Π`. Instances: `su2_hcons_zero_half_nonvacuous` (Part XVII's
  `su2_hcons_zero_half`, `β = 0`), `su2_constrained_sweep_zero_nonvacuous` (Part XVII's
  `su2_constrained_sweep_zero` annihilates a nonzero vector of `ker Π`, `β = 0`),
  `su2_influence_nonvacuous` (Part XXI's `su2_hcons_of_influence` and `su2_hsweep_of_influence`
  under `SU2HeatBathInfluence M β θ`, `0 ≤ θ < 1`, every real `β`: a nonzero `u ∈ ker Π` with
  `0 < (1/2)(1 − θ)² ‖u‖² ≤ ∑ₓ (1/16) ‖u − P_{cube2 M x ∖ Sk} u‖²` and `‖∏ P u‖ < ‖u‖` for every
  parity sweep) and `su2_hFibre_of_influence_nonvacuous` (Part X's `hFibre` through Part XXI:
  `0 < (1/2)(1 − θ)² ‖u‖² ≤ ⟪u, D u⟫`).
* `coarseY_ne_zero_one`, `su2_coarseY_ne_zero`: the coarse space `Y` is not zero at `M = 1` (the
  coarse plaquette of the single-site torus `(ℤ/1ℤ)⁴` is the commutator of two coarse links; the
  fine configuration with `diag(i, −i)` and `[[0, 1], [−1, 0]]` on two skeleton links gives
  `Re tr = −2`), hence for every `M ≥ 1` together with Part VI's `coarseY_ne_zero` (`M ≥ 2`);
  every real `β`.
* `su2_split_nontrivial` (every `M ≥ 1`, every real `β`): both `ker Π` and `ran Π` contain nonzero
  vectors of `H`.

## (c) What remains open

Everything quantitative. The named hypothesis `SU2HeatBathInfluence M β θ` of Part XXI is
proved in Lean only at `β = 0`, and `SingleLinkPoincare M β c` of Part XXII only at `β = 0`;
the `β ≠ 0` statements stay conditional on them. No lower bound on any generator at `β ≠ 0` is proved
here, the mixed block is not shown to be nonzero at any `β ≠ 0`, and the nonzero vectors constructed
here carry no estimate (no norm bound, no locality bound). Nothing here concerns uniformity in the
volume, infinite volume or a continuum limit.

## (d) Axioms and checks

Every headline depends only on `propext`, `Classical.choice` and `Quot.sound` (the module axiom
audit covers every headline); the part contains no `sorry`, `admit`, `axiom` declarations,
`native_decide`, `implemented_by` or `set_option`.

## (e) Scope

This part is not a proof of a mass gap. It shows that the finite-volume fibre and coarse spaces
of the SU(2) model are not zero, so that the conditional statements of the earlier parts are not
vacuous; it proves no gap and no new bound. "Not vacuous" means only that the hypothesis `Π u = 0`
has nonzero solutions. At `β ≠ 0` the bounds on `ker Π` remain conditional (Part XXI's
`SU2HeatBathInfluence` is established only at `β = 0`), and the vectors constructed here carry
no estimate. Physically, `ker Π ≠ 0` says that fine-scale fluctuations at fixed blocked field
exist; this holds at every coupling because `μ` has a positive density with respect to the
product Haar measure. "Every real `β`" includes `β ≤ 0` formally; the physical Wilson coupling is
`β = 4/g² > 0`. At `M = 1` the coarse torus `(ℤ/1ℤ)⁴` is a single site and each coarse link is
the holonomy of a loop winding once around the fine torus `(ℤ/2ℤ)⁴`, a degenerate case.
-/

