/-! # Part XXIX. `YangMills.StrongCoupling.SingleLinkInfluence`: the single-link Poincaré inequality of Part XXII and a direct generator bound from one named single-link influence hypothesis (new; uses Parts I, IV, VI, IX, X, XII, XV, XVI, XVIII, XXI and XXII) -/

/-!
# The single-link Poincaré inequality from a single-link influence bound

## (a) Formal target

Part XXII of this file reduces `hCoarseGap` to the named hypothesis `SingleLinkPoincare M β c`:
`c ‖u‖² ≤ ∑ₑ ‖u − P_{e} u‖²` on the centred gauge-invariant space `H` of the SU(2) Wilson measure
`μ(dU) = Z⁻¹ exp((β/2) ∑ₚ Re tr U_p) ∏ₑ dUₑ` on `(ℤ/2Mℤ)⁴`, where `β` is the Wilson coupling `β_W`
of Part VI (`κ = β/2`) and `P_{e} = E_μ[· | links ≠ e]` resamples the link `e`. Part XXI of this
file gives abstract Dobrushin-type influence data (`InfluenceBound`) and the sweep contraction they
imply. The target here is `SingleLinkPoincare` in the shape of Part XXI: one named influence
hypothesis for the single-link heat baths, satisfiable at `β = 0`, from which `SingleLinkPoincare`
and both analytic inputs of Part XXII in influence form follow.

## (b) What is proved

* Abstract (any real inner product space, any finite family of orthogonal projections, no
  commutation assumed):
  - `poincare_of_sweep`: if the sweep `Q = P_{i₁} ⋯ P_{iₙ}` along a duplicate-free list satisfies
    `‖Q u‖ ≤ θ ‖u‖` with `θ ≤ 1`, then `(1 − θ)² ‖u‖² ≤ ∑ᵢ ‖u − Pᵢ u‖²` (through Part XII's
    `norm_sub_sweepProd_sq_le`);
  - `influence_poincare`, `influence_poincare_univ`: for influence data of Part XXI with column sums
    `≤ θ`, `0 ≤ θ ≤ 1`, and a duplicate-free list whose blocks cover every coordinate, the same
    inequality holds on the closure of the domain (Part XXI's `InfluenceBound.norm_sweep_le` and
    `norm_sweep_le_of_closure`);
  - `scanAvg`, `scan_poincare` (random scan): for single-coordinate blocks `{j}`, column sums `≤ θ`,
    `θ ≥ 0`, a domain closed under linear combinations and functionals `δⱼ` that are subadditive and
    positively homogeneous there, `(1 − θ) ‖u‖² ≤ ∑ⱼ ‖u − Pⱼ u‖²` on the closure of the domain: the
    average `T = (1/n) ∑ⱼ Pⱼ` contracts `∑ⱼ δⱼ` by `1 − (1 − θ)/n`.
* SU(2) on `(ℤ/2Mℤ)⁴`, `μ ∝ exp((β/2) ∑ₚ Re tr U_p) ∏ dU`, every `M ≥ 1`, every real `β`:
  - `su2LinkPj`: the single-link projection `P_{e}` as an orthogonal projection on `H`;
  - `SU2SingleLinkInfluence M β θ`, **the named hypothesis**: an `InfluenceBound` for the
    projections `P_{e}` with the blocks `{e}` (one block per link), on a domain that is dense in `H`
    and closed under linear combinations, with subadditive and positively homogeneous `δₑ`;
  - `su2_singleLinkInfluence_zero`: it holds at `β = 0` with `θ = 0` (`D = H`,
    `δₑ f = ‖f − P_{e} f‖`, `c = 0`, `K = 1`), so it is not vacuous;
  - `su2_singleLinkPoincare_of_influence`: `SU2SingleLinkInfluence M β θ` with `θ ≥ 0` gives
    `SingleLinkPoincare M β (1 − θ)`; `su2_singleLinkPoincare_of_influence_sweep` gives the weaker
    `SingleLinkPoincare M β ((1 − θ)²)` for `0 ≤ θ ≤ 1` by the sweep route of Part XXI;
  - `su2_coarse_gap_of_linkInfluence`: `D_c ≥ ((1 − θ)/128) I` (Part XXII's
    `su2_coarse_gap_of_singleLink`);
  - `singleLinkPoincare_mono`: the constant may be lowered;
  - `su2_singleLinkPoincare_small_beta`, `su2_singleLinkPoincare_linear`,
    `su2_coarse_gap_small_beta_of_linkInfluence`: with `θ = 18 |β|`,
    `SingleLinkPoincare M β (1 − 18|β|)`, hence `SingleLinkPoincare M β (1 − 72|β|)` (the input of
    Part XXII), and `D_c ≥ ((1 − 18|β|)/128) I` (non-trivial for `|β| < 1/18`);
  - `su2_gap_small_beta_of_influences`: for `|β| ≤ 1/1000`, conditional on
    `SU2SingleLinkInfluence M β (18|β|)`, on Part XXI's `SU2HeatBathInfluence M β (228|β|)` and on the
    three local residual bounds of Part XXII's `su2_gap_small_beta_of_estimates`, the cube generator
    satisfies `D ≥ (1/230) I`;
  - `su2_gap_small_beta_of_influences_zero`: at `β = 0` every hypothesis of that theorem is
    discharged at once, so it is not vacuous;
  - comparison (`su2_gap_of_singleLink`, `su2_gap_of_linkInfluence`,
    `su2_gap_small_beta_of_linkInfluence`): the fine cube generator
    `D = ∑ₓ (1/16)(I − P_{cube2 M x})` satisfies `D ≥ (c/64) I` under `SingleLinkPoincare M β c` by a
    cover (Part XVI's `cubeGen_gap_of_cover`, `N = 32`, `m = 1/2`), hence `D ≥ ((1 − θ)/64) I` under
    `SU2SingleLinkInfluence M β θ` alone and `D ≥ ((1 − 18|β|)/64) I` with `θ = 18|β|`;
    `su2_gap_of_linkInfluence_zero` is the closed case `β = 0` (`1/64`). At `|β| ≤ 1/1000` this
    direct bound (`≥ 491/32000`) is larger than the `1/230` of `su2_gap_small_beta_of_influences`,
    which is therefore a consistency check of the Schur-split interface, not a better estimate.

## (c) What remains open

`SU2SingleLinkInfluence M β θ` is not proved here for any `β ≠ 0`, so every statement above at
`β ≠ 0` is conditional on it. The accompanying research notes give an unrefereed paper proof of
`SU2SingleLinkInfluence M β (18|β|)` for every `M ≥ 1` and every real `β`: the domain of elements
of `H` with a continuous version; `δₑ` = the oscillation in `Uₑ`; `c j e = tanh(|β| k_{je})`, where
`k_{je}` counts the plaquettes that contain both `j` and `e`; column sums at most
`|β| ∑_{j ≠ e} k_{je} = 18 |β|` (`6` plaquettes per link, `3` other links in each); `K = 1`.
`1 − 18|β| > 0` needs `|β| < 1/18` (deep strong coupling); no constant depends on `M` (uniform in
the size of the periodic torus; no infinite-volume statement). That measure theory (continuous
versions, the total-variation bound for tilted measures, density of continuous functions in `H`) is
not formalised, and neither is the count `18`. Part XXI's `SU2HeatBathInfluence` at `β ≠ 0` and the
local residual bounds of Part XXII are untouched. Nothing here concerns weak coupling.

## (d) Axioms and checks

Only `propext`, `Classical.choice` and `Quot.sound` (the module axiom audit covers every headline);
no sorry, admit, axiom declarations, native_decide or implemented_by, and no `set_option`. Uses Parts
I, IV, VI, IX, X, XII, XV, XVI, XVIII, XXI and XXII of this file.

## (e) Scope

This is not a proof of a mass gap. It is a finite-volume statement about heat-bath (single-link and
cube resampling) generators, not the transfer matrix, at deep strong coupling, conditional on named
analytic hypotheses for `β ≠ 0`. The contribution is formal: a kernel-checked derivation, inside the
interface of this file, from a named influence hypothesis. The mathematics is known on paper: under
Dobrushin's condition the heat-bath Dirichlet form `∑ᵢ ‖f − Pᵢ f‖²` has spectral gap `≥ 1 − r(C)`
for general single-spin spaces, random-scan form (L. Wu, Ann. Probab. 34 (2006) 1960–1989,
Thm 2.1); a single-link Dobrushin bound `18 β` for the SU(N) Wilson measure in `d = 4` also appears
in the preprint A. Mihajlovic, arXiv:2611.11534 (uniqueness and decay of correlations for
`β < 1/18`); the elementary tilt bound `TV ≤ tanh(osc/4)` is sharp (see the preprint Cohen–Fausti,
arXiv:2309.02413, Cor. 5.2.1), and its linear form `osc/4` goes back to Simon, Commun. Math.
Phys. 68 (1979) 183–185. Nothing here concerns weak coupling, infinite volume or the
continuum.
-/

namespace YangMills.StrongCoupling.SingleLinkInfluence

open scoped InnerProductSpace
open Finset SchurSplit YangMills.StrongCoupling.CubeSplit YangMills.StrongCoupling.CondExpInputs
  YangMills.StrongCoupling.WilsonCube YangMills.StrongCoupling.WilsonSU2
  YangMills.StrongCoupling.FibreReduction YangMills.StrongCoupling.ProductEndpoint

section Abstract

variable {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℝ H] {ι J : Type*}

/-- **Poincaré inequality from one contracting sweep.** For any finite family of orthogonal
projections `Pᵢ` (no commutation assumed), a duplicate-free list `l` and `θ ≤ 1`: if the sweep
`Q_l = ∏_{i ∈ l} Pᵢ` satisfies `‖Q_l u‖ ≤ θ ‖u‖`, then `(1 − θ)² ‖u‖² ≤ ∑ᵢ ‖u − Pᵢ u‖²`. -/
theorem poincare_of_sweep [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] (P : ι → OrthProj H) (l : List ι)
    (hl : l.Nodup) {θ : ℝ} (hθ1 : θ ≤ 1) (u : H)
    (hu : ‖ConstrainedFibre.sweepProd P l u‖ ≤ θ * ‖u‖) :
    (1 - θ) ^ 2 * ‖u‖ ^ 2 ≤ ∑ i, ‖u - (P i).P u‖ ^ 2 := by
  have h1 : (1 - θ) * ‖u‖ ≤ ‖u - ConstrainedFibre.sweepProd P l u‖ := by
    have ht := norm_sub_norm_le u (ConstrainedFibre.sweepProd P l u)
    linarith
  have h0 : 0 ≤ (1 - θ) * ‖u‖ := mul_nonneg (by linarith) (norm_nonneg u)
  have h2 := ConstrainedFibre.wmin_mul_listSum_le (fun _ => (1 : ℝ))
    (fun i => ‖u - (P i).P u‖ ^ 2) zero_le_one (fun _ => le_rfl) (fun _ => sq_nonneg _) l hl
  simp only [one_mul] at h2
  calc (1 - θ) ^ 2 * ‖u‖ ^ 2 = ((1 - θ) * ‖u‖) ^ 2 := by ring
    _ ≤ ‖u - ConstrainedFibre.sweepProd P l u‖ ^ 2 := pow_le_pow_left₀ h0 h1 2
    _ ≤ (l.map fun i => ‖u - (P i).P u‖ ^ 2).sum :=
        ConstrainedFibre.norm_sub_sweepProd_sq_le P u l
    _ ≤ ∑ i, ‖u - (P i).P u‖ ^ 2 := h2

variable [Fintype J] [DecidableEq J] {P : ι → OrthProj H} {B : ι → Finset J} {θ : ℝ}

/-- **Poincaré inequality from influence data.** Influence data of Part XXI with column sums `≤ θ`,
`0 ≤ θ ≤ 1`, and a duplicate-free list `l` whose blocks cover every coordinate give
`(1 − θ)² ‖u‖² ≤ ∑ᵢ ‖u − Pᵢ u‖²` for every `u` in the closure of the domain. -/
theorem influence_poincare [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι]
    (I : SweepContraction.InfluenceBound P B θ) (hθ0 : 0 ≤ θ) (hθ1 : θ ≤ 1) (l : List ι)
    (hl : l.Nodup) (hcov : ∀ j, ∃ i ∈ l, j ∈ B i) (u : H) (hu : u ∈ closure I.D) :
    (1 - θ) ^ 2 * ‖u‖ ^ 2 ≤ ∑ i, ‖u - (P i).P u‖ ^ 2 :=
  poincare_of_sweep P l hl hθ1 u
    (SweepContraction.norm_sweep_le_of_closure P l I.D
      (fun f hf => I.norm_sweep_le hθ0 hθ1 l hcov f hf) u hu)

/-- **The same with the sweep over all blocks** (`l = Finset.univ.toList`): if every coordinate lies
in some block and the domain is dense, `(1 − θ)² ‖u‖² ≤ ∑ᵢ ‖u − Pᵢ u‖²` for every `u`. -/
theorem influence_poincare_univ [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι]
    (I : SweepContraction.InfluenceBound P B θ) (hθ0 : 0 ≤ θ) (hθ1 : θ ≤ 1)
    (hcov : ∀ j, ∃ i, j ∈ B i) (hdense : ∀ u, u ∈ closure I.D) (u : H) :
    (1 - θ) ^ 2 * ‖u‖ ^ 2 ≤ ∑ i, ‖u - (P i).P u‖ ^ 2 :=
  influence_poincare I hθ0 hθ1 (Finset.univ : Finset ι).toList (Finset.nodup_toList _)
    (fun j => by
      obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := hcov j
      exact ⟨i, Finset.mem_toList.2 (Finset.mem_univ i), hi⟩) u (hdense u)

end Abstract

section RandomScan

variable {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℝ H] {J : Type*} [Fintype J]

/-- The random-scan average `T = (1/n) ∑ⱼ Pⱼ` (`n = card J`). -/
noncomputable def scanAvg (P : J → OrthProj H) : H →ₗ[ℝ] H :=
  ((Fintype.card J : ℝ)⁻¹) • ∑ j, (P j).P

theorem scanAvg_apply (P : J → OrthProj H) (x : H) :
    scanAvg P x = ((Fintype.card J : ℝ)⁻¹) • ∑ j, (P j).P x := by
  simp [scanAvg, LinearMap.sum_apply]

theorem scanAvg_isSymmetric (P : J → OrthProj H) : (scanAvg P).IsSymmetric := by
  intro x y
  rw [scanAvg_apply, scanAvg_apply, real_inner_smul_left, real_inner_smul_right, sum_inner,
    inner_sum]
  congr 1
  exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => (P j).symm x y

/-- `⟪x, T x⟫ = ‖x‖² − (1/n) ∑ⱼ ‖x − Pⱼ x‖²`. -/
theorem inner_scanAvg [Nonempty J] (P : J → OrthProj H) (x : H) :
    ⟪x, scanAvg P x⟫_ℝ = ‖x‖ ^ 2 - (Fintype.card J : ℝ)⁻¹ * ∑ j, ‖x - (P j).P x‖ ^ 2 := by
  have hn : (Fintype.card J : ℝ) ≠ 0 := by exact_mod_cast (Fintype.card_pos (α := J)).ne'
  have h : ∀ j, ⟪x, (P j).P x⟫_ℝ = ‖x‖ ^ 2 - ‖x - (P j).P x‖ ^ 2 := fun j => by
    rw [(P j).inner_P_self x]
    linarith [(P j).norm_sq_split x]
  rw [scanAvg_apply, real_inner_smul_right, inner_sum, Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => h j,
    Finset.sum_sub_distrib, Finset.sum_const, Finset.card_univ, nsmul_eq_mul, mul_sub,
    ← mul_assoc, inv_mul_cancel₀ hn, one_mul]

/-- **Poincaré inequality `1 − θ` from single-coordinate influence data (random scan).** Let
`Pⱼ` (`j ∈ J`, `J` finite and nonempty) be orthogonal projections with influence data of Part XXI for
the blocks `{j}` and column sums `≤ θ`, `θ ≥ 0`, on a domain `D` that contains `0` and is closed
under addition and real scalar multiplication, with each `δⱼ` subadditive and positively homogeneous
on `D`. Then `(1 − θ) ‖u‖² ≤ ∑ⱼ ‖u − Pⱼ u‖²` on the closure of `D` (non-trivial for `θ < 1`). The
proof: `T = (1/n) ∑ⱼ Pⱼ` contracts `∑ⱼ δⱼ` by `r = 1 − (1 − θ)/n` on `D`, so `‖T f‖ ≤ r ‖f‖`
(Part X's `norm_apply_le_of_pow_decay`), and `⟪f, T f⟫ = ‖f‖² − (1/n) ∑ⱼ ‖f − Pⱼ f‖²`. -/
theorem scan_poincare [DecidableEq J] [Nonempty J] {P : J → OrthProj H} {θ : ℝ}
    (I : SweepContraction.InfluenceBound P (fun j => ({j} : Finset J)) θ) (hθ0 : 0 ≤ θ)
    (hzero : (0 : H) ∈ I.D) (hadd : ∀ f ∈ I.D, ∀ g ∈ I.D, f + g ∈ I.D)
    (hsmul : ∀ (a : ℝ), ∀ f ∈ I.D, a • f ∈ I.D)
    (hδadd : ∀ j, ∀ f ∈ I.D, ∀ g ∈ I.D, I.δ j (f + g) ≤ I.δ j f + I.δ j g)
    (hδsmul : ∀ j (a : ℝ), 0 ≤ a → ∀ f ∈ I.D, I.δ j (a • f) ≤ a * I.δ j f)
    (u : H) (hu : u ∈ closure I.D) :
    (1 - θ) * ‖u‖ ^ 2 ≤ ∑ j, ‖u - (P j).P u‖ ^ 2 := by
  have hn : (0 : ℝ) < Fintype.card J := by exact_mod_cast (Fintype.card_pos (α := J))
  have hn1 : (1 : ℝ) ≤ Fintype.card J := by
    exact_mod_cast Nat.succ_le_of_lt (Fintype.card_pos (α := J))
  set n : ℝ := (Fintype.card J : ℝ) with hn_def
  set r : ℝ := 1 - (1 - θ) / n with hr_def
  have hr0 : 0 ≤ r := by
    rw [hr_def, sub_nonneg, div_le_one hn]
    linarith
  have hδ0 : ∀ j, I.δ j 0 ≤ 0 := fun j => by
    have h := hδsmul j 0 le_rfl 0 hzero
    rwa [smul_zero, zero_mul] at h
  -- one step of `T`
  have hstep : ∀ f ∈ I.D, scanAvg P f ∈ I.D ∧
      ∑ j, I.δ j (scanAvg P f) ≤ r * ∑ j, I.δ j f := by
    intro f hf
    have hPf : ∀ i, (P i).P f ∈ I.D := fun i => I.mem i f hf
    have hsum : (∑ i, (P i).P f) ∈ I.D :=
      Finset.sum_induction _ (· ∈ I.D) (fun a b ha hb => hadd a ha b hb) hzero
        (fun i _ => hPf i)
    refine ⟨by rw [scanAvg_apply]; exact hsmul _ _ hsum, ?_⟩
    -- per-coordinate bound
    have hcoord : ∀ j, I.δ j (scanAvg P f) ≤ n⁻¹ * ∑ i, I.δ j ((P i).P f) := fun j => by
      rw [scanAvg_apply]
      refine (hδsmul j _ (inv_nonneg.2 hn.le) _ hsum).trans ?_
      refine mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left ?_ (inv_nonneg.2 hn.le)
      exact Finset.le_sum_of_subadditive_on_pred (I.δ j) (· ∈ I.D) (hδ0 j)
        (fun x y hx hy => hδadd j x hx y hy) (fun x y hx hy => hadd x hx y hy) _
        (fun i _ => hPf i)
    -- per-block bound: `∑ⱼ δⱼ(Pᵢ f) ≤ S − (1 − θ) δᵢ f`
    have hblock : ∀ i, ∑ j, I.δ j ((P i).P f) ≤ ∑ j, I.δ j f - (1 - θ) * I.δ i f := fun i => by
      rw [← Finset.sum_add_sum_compl ({i} : Finset J) (fun j => I.δ j ((P i).P f)),
        ← Finset.sum_add_sum_compl ({i} : Finset J) (fun j => I.δ j f),
        Finset.sum_singleton, Finset.sum_singleton,
        I.self i i (Finset.mem_singleton_self i) f hf]
      have h1 : ∑ j ∈ ({i} : Finset J)ᶜ, I.δ j ((P i).P f) ≤
          ∑ j ∈ ({i} : Finset J)ᶜ, (I.δ j f + I.c j i * I.δ i f) :=
        Finset.sum_le_sum fun j hj => by
          have := I.infl i j (Finset.mem_compl.1 hj) f hf
          rwa [Finset.sum_singleton] at this
      rw [Finset.sum_add_distrib, ← Finset.sum_mul] at h1
      have h2 : (∑ j ∈ ({i} : Finset J)ᶜ, I.c j i) * I.δ i f ≤ θ * I.δ i f :=
        mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right (I.col i) (I.nonneg i f hf)
      linarith
    have hS0 : ∀ i, 0 ≤ I.δ i f := fun i => I.nonneg i f hf
    calc ∑ j, I.δ j (scanAvg P f) ≤ ∑ j, n⁻¹ * ∑ i, I.δ j ((P i).P f) :=
          Finset.sum_le_sum fun j _ => hcoord j
      _ = n⁻¹ * ∑ i, ∑ j, I.δ j ((P i).P f) := by rw [← Finset.mul_sum, Finset.sum_comm]
      _ ≤ n⁻¹ * ∑ i, (∑ j, I.δ j f - (1 - θ) * I.δ i f) :=
          mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left (Finset.sum_le_sum fun i _ => hblock i)
            (inv_nonneg.2 hn.le)
      _ = r * ∑ j, I.δ j f := by
          rw [Finset.sum_sub_distrib, Finset.sum_const, Finset.card_univ, nsmul_eq_mul,
            ← Finset.mul_sum, hr_def, ← hn_def]
          field_simp
  -- the Poincaré inequality on `D`
  have hD : ∀ f ∈ I.D, (1 - θ) * ‖f‖ ^ 2 ≤ ∑ j, ‖f - (P j).P f‖ ^ 2 := by
    intro f hf
    have hpow : ∀ m : ℕ, (scanAvg P ^ m) f ∈ I.D ∧
        ∑ j, I.δ j ((scanAvg P ^ m) f) ≤ r ^ m * ∑ j, I.δ j f := by
      intro m
      induction m with
      | zero => simp [hf]
      | succ m ih =>
        rw [pow_succ' (scanAvg P) m, Module.End.mul_apply]
        obtain ⟨h1, h2⟩ := hstep _ ih.1
        refine ⟨h1, h2.trans ?_⟩
        rw [pow_succ' r m, mul_assoc]
        exact mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left ih.2 hr0
    have hdec : ∀ m : ℕ, ‖(scanAvg P ^ m) f‖ ≤ (I.K * ∑ j, I.δ j f) * r ^ m := fun m =>
      calc ‖(scanAvg P ^ m) f‖ ≤ I.K * ∑ j, I.δ j ((scanAvg P ^ m) f) := I.poinc _ (hpow m).1
        _ ≤ I.K * (r ^ m * ∑ j, I.δ j f) := mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left (hpow m).2 I.K_nonneg
        _ = (I.K * ∑ j, I.δ j f) * r ^ m := by ring
    have hTf := FibreReduction.norm_apply_le_of_pow_decay (scanAvg P) (scanAvg_isSymmetric P) f
      hr0 hdec
    have hin : ⟪f, scanAvg P f⟫_ℝ ≤ r * ‖f‖ ^ 2 :=
      calc ⟪f, scanAvg P f⟫_ℝ ≤ ‖f‖ * ‖scanAvg P f‖ := real_inner_le_norm _ _
        _ ≤ ‖f‖ * (r * ‖f‖) := mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left hTf (norm_nonneg f)
        _ = r * ‖f‖ ^ 2 := by ring
    rw [inner_scanAvg P f, hr_def] at hin
    have h3 : n⁻¹ * ((1 - θ) * ‖f‖ ^ 2) ≤ n⁻¹ * ∑ j, ‖f - (P j).P f‖ ^ 2 := by
      have e : n⁻¹ * ((1 - θ) * ‖f‖ ^ 2) = (1 - θ) / n * ‖f‖ ^ 2 := by ring
      rw [e]
      linarith
    exact le_of_mul_le_mul_left h3 (inv_pos.2 hn)
  -- closure
  have hcont : ∀ j, Continuous (P j).P := fun j =>
    AddMonoidHomClass.continuous_of_bound (P j).P 1 fun x => by
      rw [one_mul]
      exact SweepContraction.norm_P_le (P j) x
  have hclosed : IsClosed {v : H | (1 - θ) * ‖v‖ ^ 2 ≤ ∑ j, ‖v - (P j).P v‖ ^ 2} :=
    isClosed_le (continuous_const.mul (continuous_norm.pow 2))
      (continuous_finsetSum _ fun j _ => (continuous_id.sub (hcont j)).norm.pow 2)
  exact closure_minimal hD hclosed hu

end RandomScan

/-! ### SU(2) on `(ℤ/2Mℤ)⁴`, `μ ∝ exp((β/2) ∑ₚ Re tr U_p) ∏ dU`: the single-link heat baths -/

section SU2

variable (M : ℕ) [NeZero M]

/-- The single-link projection `P_{e} = E_μ[· | links ≠ e]` on `H`, as an orthogonal projection, for
the SU(2) Wilson measure `μ ∝ exp((β/2) ∑ₚ Re tr U_p) ∏ dU` on `(ℤ/2Mℤ)⁴`. -/
noncomputable abbrev su2LinkPj (β : ℝ) (e : Link (2 * M)) :
    OrthProj (wilsonH (plaqOf (n := 2 * M)) reTr (β / 2) haarSU2) :=
  wilsonPj (plaqOf (n := 2 * M)) reTr (β / 2) haarSU2 {e}

/-- **The single-link analytic input, as one named hypothesis.** Dobrushin influence data (Part XXI's
`InfluenceBound`) for the single-link heat baths `P_{e}` of the SU(2) Wilson measure
`μ ∝ exp((β/2) ∑ₚ Re tr U_p) ∏ dU` on `(ℤ/2Mℤ)⁴`, one block `{e}` per link: functionals `δₑ ≥ 0`
killed by `P_{e}`, `δⱼ(P_{e} f) ≤ δⱼ f + c j e · δₑ f` for `j ≠ e`, column sums
`∑_{j ≠ e} c j e ≤ θ` and `‖f‖ ≤ K ∑ⱼ δⱼ f`, on a domain that is dense in `H` and closed under linear
combinations, with each `δⱼ` subadditive and positively homogeneous there. Intended instance
(paper): the elements of `H` with a continuous version, `δⱼ` = the oscillation in `Uⱼ`,
`c j e = tanh(|β| k_{je})` with `k_{je}` the number of plaquettes containing `j` and `e`,
`θ = 18 |β|`, `K = 1`, for every `M ≥ 1` and every real `β`. That instance is not formalised; the
Lean instance is `su2_singleLinkInfluence_zero` (`β = 0`, `θ = 0`). -/
structure SU2SingleLinkInfluence (β θ : ℝ) extends
    SweepContraction.InfluenceBound (su2LinkPj M β)
      (fun e : Link (2 * M) => ({e} : Finset (Link (2 * M)))) θ where
  /-- The domain is dense in `H`. -/
  dense : ∀ u, u ∈ closure D
  /-- The domain contains `0`. -/
  zero_mem : (0 : wilsonH (plaqOf (n := 2 * M)) reTr (β / 2) haarSU2) ∈ D
  /-- The domain is closed under addition. -/
  add_mem : ∀ f ∈ D, ∀ g ∈ D, f + g ∈ D
  /-- The domain is closed under real scalar multiplication. -/
  smul_mem : ∀ (a : ℝ), ∀ f ∈ D, a • f ∈ D
  /-- Each `δⱼ` is subadditive on the domain. -/
  δ_add : ∀ j, ∀ f ∈ D, ∀ g ∈ D, δ j (f + g) ≤ δ j f + δ j g
  /-- Each `δⱼ` is positively homogeneous on the domain. -/
  δ_smul : ∀ j (a : ℝ), 0 ≤ a → ∀ f ∈ D, δ j (a • f) ≤ a * δ j f

variable {M}

/-- **`SingleLinkPoincare` from the single-link influence hypothesis** (SU(2) on `(ℤ/2Mℤ)⁴`,
`μ ∝ exp((β/2) ∑ₚ Re tr U_p) ∏ dU`, every `M ≥ 1`, every real `β`, `θ ≥ 0`; conditional on
`SU2SingleLinkInfluence M β θ`): `(1 − θ) ‖u‖² ≤ ∑ₑ ‖u − P_{e} u‖²` on `H` (random scan,
`scan_poincare`; non-trivial for `θ < 1`). -/
theorem su2_singleLinkPoincare_of_influence {β θ : ℝ} (I : SU2SingleLinkInfluence M β θ)
    (hθ0 : 0 ≤ θ) : SmallCouplingInputs.SingleLinkPoincare M β (1 - θ) :=
  fun u => scan_poincare I.toInfluenceBound hθ0 I.zero_mem I.add_mem I.smul_mem I.δ_add I.δ_smul u
    (I.dense u)

/-- **The sweep route** (every `M ≥ 1`, every real `β`, `0 ≤ θ ≤ 1`; conditional on
`SU2SingleLinkInfluence M β θ`, using only its `InfluenceBound` and density fields): the sweep of
Part XXI over all links gives the weaker `SingleLinkPoincare M β ((1 − θ)²)`. -/
theorem su2_singleLinkPoincare_of_influence_sweep {β θ : ℝ} (I : SU2SingleLinkInfluence M β θ)
    (hθ0 : 0 ≤ θ) (hθ1 : θ ≤ 1) : SmallCouplingInputs.SingleLinkPoincare M β ((1 - θ) ^ 2) :=
  fun u => influence_poincare_univ I.toInfluenceBound hθ0 hθ1
    (fun j => ⟨j, Finset.mem_singleton_self j⟩) I.dense u

/-- **`hCoarseGap` from the single-link influence hypothesis** (every `M ≥ 1`, every real `β`,
`θ ≥ 0`, coarse side-2 cubes at every coarse base point with weights `1/16`; conditional on
`SU2SingleLinkInfluence M β θ`): `D_c ≥ ((1 − θ)/128) I` (non-trivial for `θ < 1`). -/
theorem su2_coarse_gap_of_linkInfluence {β θ : ℝ} (I : SU2SingleLinkInfluence M β θ)
    (hθ0 : 0 ≤ θ) :
    ((1 - θ) / 128) • LinearMap.id ≤ su2Dc M β (sideTwoCube M) (fun _ => 1 / 16) :=
  SmallCouplingInputs.su2_coarse_gap_of_singleLink M β (su2_singleLinkPoincare_of_influence I hθ0)

/-- `SingleLinkPoincare M β c'` implies `SingleLinkPoincare M β c` for `c ≤ c'`. -/
theorem singleLinkPoincare_mono {β c c' : ℝ} (hcc : c ≤ c')
    (h : SmallCouplingInputs.SingleLinkPoincare M β c') :
    SmallCouplingInputs.SingleLinkPoincare M β c := fun u =>
  (mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right hcc (sq_nonneg ‖u‖)).trans (h u)

/-- **`SingleLinkPoincare` at small coupling** (every `M ≥ 1`, every real `β`, non-trivial for
`|β| < 1/18`; conditional on `SU2SingleLinkInfluence M β (18 |β|)`):
`SingleLinkPoincare M β (1 − 18|β|)`. -/
theorem su2_singleLinkPoincare_small_beta {β : ℝ} (I : SU2SingleLinkInfluence M β (18 * |β|)) :
    SmallCouplingInputs.SingleLinkPoincare M β (1 - 18 * |β|) :=
  su2_singleLinkPoincare_of_influence I (by positivity)

/-- **The input of Part XXII** (every `M ≥ 1`, every real `β`; conditional on
`SU2SingleLinkInfluence M β (18 |β|)`): `SingleLinkPoincare M β (1 − 72|β|)`. -/
theorem su2_singleLinkPoincare_linear {β : ℝ} (I : SU2SingleLinkInfluence M β (18 * |β|)) :
    SmallCouplingInputs.SingleLinkPoincare M β (1 - 72 * |β|) :=
  singleLinkPoincare_mono (by linarith [abs_nonneg β]) (su2_singleLinkPoincare_small_beta I)

/-- **`hCoarseGap` at small coupling** (every `M ≥ 1`, every real `β`, non-trivial for
`|β| < 1/18`; conditional on `SU2SingleLinkInfluence M β (18 |β|)`):
`D_c ≥ ((1 − 18|β|)/128) I`. -/
theorem su2_coarse_gap_small_beta_of_linkInfluence {β : ℝ}
    (I : SU2SingleLinkInfluence M β (18 * |β|)) :
    ((1 - 18 * |β|) / 128) • LinearMap.id ≤ su2Dc M β (sideTwoCube M) (fun _ => 1 / 16) :=
  su2_coarse_gap_of_linkInfluence (θ := 18 * |β|) I (by positivity)

/-- **The cube generator at small coupling, with both analytic inputs of Part XXII in influence
form** (SU(2) on `(ℤ/2Mℤ)⁴`, `d = 4`, every `M ≥ 1`, `|β| ≤ 1/1000` in the normalisation of Part
VI's `su2Wilson`, straight blocking, fine side-2 cubes `cube2 M x` and coarse side-2 cubes
`sideTwoCube M z` at every base point, all weights `1/16`). Conditional on
`SU2SingleLinkInfluence M β (18|β|)` (which gives `SingleLinkPoincare M β (1 − 72|β|)`), on Part
XXI's `SweepContraction.SU2HeatBathInfluence M β (228|β|)` (which gives `hcons`) and on the three
local residual bounds of Part XXII's `su2_gap_small_beta_of_estimates` (`Γ ≥ 0`, `hB`, `hg`, `hC`):
`D ≥ (1/230) I`. No constant depends on `M`. This is an implication between named hypotheses, none
of which is proved here for `β ≠ 0`; a finite-volume heat-bath bound, not a mass gap. Under the
single-link hypothesis alone, `su2_gap_small_beta_of_linkInfluence` gives the larger
`D ≥ ((1 − 18|β|)/64) I`; this theorem is a consistency check of the Schur-split interface. -/
theorem su2_gap_small_beta_of_influences {β : ℝ} (hβ : |β| ≤ 1 / 1000)
    (Ilink : SU2SingleLinkInfluence M β (18 * |β|))
    (Iheat : SweepContraction.SU2HeatBathInfluence M β (228 * |β|))
    (Γ : (su2Pi M β).Hc → ℝ) (hΓ : ∀ v, 0 ≤ Γ v)
    (hB : ∀ v, ‖(su2Pi M β).blkB (su2D M β (cube2 M) (fun _ => 1 / 16)) v‖ ^ 2 ≤
      63 / 2 * (Real.exp (12 * |β|) - 1) ^ 2 * Real.exp (108 * |β|) / (1 - 72 * |β|) * Γ v)
    (hg : ∀ v, (su2Pi M β).gC (su2Jt M β) (su2Dc M β (sideTwoCube M) (fun _ => 1 / 16)) v ≤
      Real.exp (576 * |β|) / 2 * Γ v)
    (hC : ∀ v, (1 - ((Real.exp (36 * |β|) - 1) * Real.exp (18 * |β|)) ^ 2) * Γ v ≤
      ⟪v, (su2Pi M β).blkC (su2D M β (cube2 M) (fun _ => 1 / 16)) v⟫_ℝ) :
    (1 / 230 : ℝ) • LinearMap.id ≤ su2D M β (cube2 M) (fun _ => 1 / 16) :=
  SmallCouplingInputs.su2_gap_small_beta_of_influence M β hβ Iheat
    (su2_singleLinkPoincare_linear Ilink) Γ hΓ hB hg hC

/-! #### Comparison: the fine cube generator directly from the single-link inequality -/

/-- **The fine cube generator from `SingleLinkPoincare` by a cover** (every `M ≥ 1`, every real `β`,
fine side-2 cubes `cube2 M x` at every base point with weights `1/16`; conditional on
`SingleLinkPoincare M β c`): `D ≥ (c/64) I` on `H`. Each fine cube has at most `32` links and each
fine link lies in `8` fine cubes (Part XXII's counts on `(ℤ/2Mℤ)⁴`, `2M ≥ 2`), so Part XVI's
`cubeGen_gap_of_cover` applies with `N = 32`, `m = 1/2`. A finite-volume lower bound for the
heat-bath generator, not a mass gap. -/
theorem su2_gap_of_singleLink {β c : ℝ} (hfine : SmallCouplingInputs.SingleLinkPoincare M β c) :
    (c / 64) • LinearMap.id ≤ su2D M β (cube2 M) (fun _ => 1 / 16) := by
  have h : ((1 / 2 : ℝ) / 32 * c) • LinearMap.id ≤ su2D M β (cube2 M) (fun _ => 1 / 16) :=
    SmallCoupling.cubeGen_gap_of_cover (fun _ => 1 / 16) (fun _ => by norm_num)
      (fun x => wilsonPj (plaqOf (n := 2 * M)) reTr (β / 2) haarSU2 (cube2 M x)) (su2LinkPj M β)
      (SmallCouplingInputs.cubeLinkFinset (2 * M)) (by norm_num) (by norm_num)
      (fun x => by exact_mod_cast SmallCouplingInputs.card_cubeLinkFinset_le (2 * M) x)
      (fun x j hj z => wilsonP_fixes_wilsonP _ _ _ _
        (Set.singleton_subset_iff.2 ((SmallCouplingInputs.mem_cubeLinkFinset (2 * M) x j).1 hj)) z)
      (fun j => (SmallCouplingInputs.cover_weight (2 * M)
        (by have := NeZero.ne M; omega) j).ge) hfine
  have e : c / 64 = (1 / 2 : ℝ) / 32 * c := by ring
  exact (congrArg (fun t : ℝ => t • (LinearMap.id : wilsonH (plaqOf (n := 2 * M)) reTr (β / 2)
    haarSU2 →ₗ[ℝ] wilsonH (plaqOf (n := 2 * M)) reTr (β / 2) haarSU2)) e).trans_le h

/-- **The fine cube generator from the single-link influence hypothesis alone** (every `M ≥ 1`,
every real `β`, `θ ≥ 0`, fine side-2 cubes, weights `1/16`; conditional on
`SU2SingleLinkInfluence M β θ` only): `D ≥ ((1 − θ)/64) I` on `H` (non-trivial for `θ < 1`). A
finite-volume lower bound for
the heat-bath generator, not a mass gap. -/
theorem su2_gap_of_linkInfluence {β θ : ℝ} (I : SU2SingleLinkInfluence M β θ) (hθ0 : 0 ≤ θ) :
    ((1 - θ) / 64) • LinearMap.id ≤ su2D M β (cube2 M) (fun _ => 1 / 16) :=
  su2_gap_of_singleLink (su2_singleLinkPoincare_of_influence I hθ0)

/-- **The same at small coupling** (every `M ≥ 1`, every real `β`, non-trivial for `|β| < 1/18`;
conditional on `SU2SingleLinkInfluence M β (18 |β|)` only): `D ≥ ((1 − 18|β|)/64) I` on `H`. For
`|β| ≤ 1/1000` this is at least `(491/500)/64 > 1/230`. -/
theorem su2_gap_small_beta_of_linkInfluence {β : ℝ} (I : SU2SingleLinkInfluence M β (18 * |β|)) :
    ((1 - 18 * |β|) / 64) • LinearMap.id ≤ su2D M β (cube2 M) (fun _ => 1 / 16) :=
  su2_gap_of_linkInfluence (θ := 18 * |β|) I (by positivity)

/-! #### Non-vacuity at `β = 0` -/

variable (M)

/-- **The named hypothesis holds at `β = 0` with `θ = 0`** (every `M ≥ 1`): `D = H`,
`δₑ f = ‖f − P_{e} f‖` (a seminorm), `c = 0`, `K = 1` (the comparison from Part XXII's
`singleLinkPoincare_zero`). So `SU2SingleLinkInfluence` is not vacuous. -/
noncomputable def su2_singleLinkInfluence_zero : SU2SingleLinkInfluence M 0 0 where
  D := Set.univ
  δ e f := ‖f - su2P M 0 {e} f‖
  c _ _ := 0
  K := 1
  mem _ _ _ := Set.mem_univ _
  nonneg _ _ _ := norm_nonneg _
  self i j hj f _ :=
    SweepContraction.single_fixes M 0 (V := {i}) (e := j) (Finset.mem_singleton.1 hj) f
  infl i j _ f _ := by
    simp only [zero_mul, add_zero]
    exact SweepContraction.single_infl_zero M {i} j f
  c_nonneg _ _ := le_rfl
  col _ := by simp
  K_nonneg := zero_le_one
  poinc f _ := by
    have h1 := SmallCouplingInputs.singleLinkPoincare_zero M f
    have h2 := Finset.sum_sq_le_sq_sum_of_nonneg (s := (Finset.univ : Finset (Link (2 * M))))
      (f := fun e => ‖f - su2P M 0 {e} f‖) (fun _ _ => norm_nonneg _)
    have h3 : 0 ≤ ∑ e, ‖f - su2P M 0 {e} f‖ := Finset.sum_nonneg fun _ _ => norm_nonneg _
    exact le_of_le_of_eq ((pow_le_pow_iff_left₀ (norm_nonneg f) h3 two_ne_zero).1
      (((le_of_eq (one_mul (‖f‖ ^ 2)).symm).trans h1).trans h2)) (one_mul _).symm
  dense _ := subset_closure (Set.mem_univ _)
  zero_mem := Set.mem_univ _
  add_mem _ _ _ _ := Set.mem_univ _
  smul_mem _ _ _ := Set.mem_univ _
  δ_add j f _ g _ := by
    have e : f + g - su2P M 0 {j} (f + g) = (f - su2P M 0 {j} f) + (g - su2P M 0 {j} g) := by
      rw [(su2P M 0 {j}).map_add f g]
      abel
    rw [e]
    exact norm_add_le _ _
  δ_smul j a ha f _ := by
    refine le_of_eq ?_
    rw [(su2P M 0 {j}).map_smul a f, ← smul_sub a f (su2P M 0 {j} f), norm_smul_of_nonneg ha]

/-- `SU2SingleLinkInfluence M 0 (18 |0|)` is inhabited (every `M ≥ 1`): the small-coupling form of
the hypothesis is satisfiable at `β = 0`. -/
theorem su2_singleLinkInfluence_zero_nonempty :
    Nonempty (SU2SingleLinkInfluence M 0 (18 * |(0 : ℝ)|)) := by
  rw [abs_zero, mul_zero]
  exact ⟨su2_singleLinkInfluence_zero M⟩

/-- **Non-vacuity of `su2_gap_small_beta_of_influences`** (every `M ≥ 1`, `β = 0`): all its
hypotheses are discharged at once (`su2_singleLinkInfluence_zero`; Part XXI's `su2_influence_zero`;
`Γ v = ⟪v, C v⟫` with Part XV's `su2_blkB_zero` and Part XVIII's `su2_gC_le_zero`), so it returns
`D ≥ (1/230) I`. The elementary bound at `β = 0` is larger; this only shows the hypotheses can be
met simultaneously. -/
theorem su2_gap_small_beta_of_influences_zero :
    (1 / 230 : ℝ) • LinearMap.id ≤ su2D M 0 (cube2 M) (fun _ => 1 / 16) := by
  have ha : |(0 : ℝ)| = 0 := abs_zero
  have hCG0 := SchurTower.form_of_smul_id_le (su2_coarse_gap_zero M)
  have hgC : ∀ v : (su2Pi M 0).Hc,
      0 ≤ (su2Pi M 0).gC (su2Jt M 0) (su2Dc M 0 (sideTwoCube M) (fun _ => 1 / 16)) v := by
    intro v
    exact le_trans (by positivity) (hCG0 (su2Jt M 0 v))
  have Ilink : SU2SingleLinkInfluence M 0 (18 * |(0 : ℝ)|) := by
    rw [ha, mul_zero]
    exact su2_singleLinkInfluence_zero M
  have Iheat : SweepContraction.SU2HeatBathInfluence M 0 (228 * |(0 : ℝ)|) := by
    rw [ha, mul_zero]
    exact SweepContraction.su2_influence_zero M
  refine su2_gap_small_beta_of_influences (by rw [ha]; norm_num) Ilink Iheat
    (fun v => ⟪v, (su2Pi M 0).blkC (su2D M 0 (cube2 M) (fun _ => 1 / 16)) v⟫_ℝ)
    (fun v => ?_) (fun v => ?_) (fun v => ?_) (fun v => ?_)
  · have h1 := UniformEndpoint.su2_gC_le_zero M v
    have h2 := hgC v
    linarith
  · have h0 : ‖(su2Pi M 0).blkB (su2D M 0 (cube2 M) (fun _ => 1 / 16)) v‖ ^ 2 = 0 := by
      rw [su2_blkB_zero M v]
      simp
    calc ‖(su2Pi M 0).blkB (su2D M 0 (cube2 M) (fun _ => 1 / 16)) v‖ ^ 2 = 0 := h0
      _ ≤ _ := by simp
  · have h1 := UniformEndpoint.su2_gC_le_zero M v
    simp only [ha, mul_zero, Real.exp_zero]
    linarith
  · simp only [ha, mul_zero, Real.exp_zero, sub_self, zero_mul]
    norm_num

/-- **The direct chain at `β = 0`, closed** (every `M ≥ 1`): `su2_singleLinkInfluence_zero` and
`su2_gap_of_linkInfluence` give `D ≥ (1/64) I`, so that theorem is not vacuous. -/
theorem su2_gap_of_linkInfluence_zero :
    (1 / 64 : ℝ) • LinearMap.id ≤ su2D M 0 (cube2 M) (fun _ => 1 / 16) := by
  have h := su2_gap_of_linkInfluence (su2_singleLinkInfluence_zero M) le_rfl
  have e : (1 / 64 : ℝ) = (1 - 0) / 64 := by norm_num
  exact (congrArg (fun t : ℝ => t • (LinearMap.id : wilsonH (plaqOf (n := 2 * M)) reTr ((0 : ℝ) / 2)
    haarSU2 →ₗ[ℝ] wilsonH (plaqOf (n := 2 * M)) reTr ((0 : ℝ) / 2) haarSU2)) e).trans_le h

end SU2

end YangMills.StrongCoupling.SingleLinkInfluence

/-! # Part XXX. `YangMills.StrongCoupling.HeatBathKernel`: the heat-bath kernel of the Wilson measure, i.e. the conditional law of one link or of a block of links given the other links, its continuity, and the SU(2) instances (new; uses Parts III, IV, VI, X and XXIX) -/

/-!
# The heat-bath kernels of the Wilson measure: conditional expectations given the links outside a set

## (a) Formal target

Part IV of this file defines the finite-volume Wilson measure
`μ = (∏ₑ h)` tilted by `wilsonExp plaq χ κ` (density `Z⁻¹ exp(κ ∑ₚ χ(U_p))`), the exterior
σ-algebras `extSigma V` (the links outside `V`) and the heat-bath projections
`wilsonP V = E_μ[· | extSigma V]` on the centred gauge-invariant space `H`. The target here is the
explicit conditional law: for a bounded measurable `g`, `E_μ[g | links ≠ e]` is (almost everywhere)
the average of `g` over the link `e` against `h` tilted by the Wilson exponent with the other links
frozen, and the
same for a set `V` of links (block heat bath); for a compact topological group (first countable for
one link, second countable for a block) and continuous `g`, `χ` these averages are continuous. For
SU(2) on `(ℤ/2Mℤ)⁴` (`κ = β/2`, `β = β_W`, `χ = Re tr`, Haar measure)
this gives continuous versions of `P_{e} f` and of `P_V f` whenever `f` has one.

## (b) What is proved

* Abstract resampling engine (any probability spaces `Ω`, `Ξ`): if `R : Ω × Ξ → Ω` pushes
  `ν₀ ⊗ ρ` to `ν₀`, factors through a projection `pr` with `m = σ(pr)` (`m ≤ σ(pr)`, `pr`
  `m`-measurable), then for every bounded measurable `w`, `g`,
  `(ν₀.tilted w)[g | m] = U ↦ ∫ g(R(U, ξ)) d(ρ.tilted (w ∘ R(U, ·)))(ξ)` almost everywhere
  (`condExp_resample`, through the exchange identity `integral_mul_resample`).
* `blockUpd V W U` (`U` updated on `V` by `W`), the pushforwards `map_update` and `map_blockUpd`
  (`∏ h` is invariant under resampling one link or a block), `extSigma V = σ(U ↦ blockUpd V 1 U)`
  in the form needed by the engine.
* Single link, generic Wilson setting (finite `E`, any measurable group `G`, probability `h`, any
  plaquettes, any class function `χ`, any real `κ`): `kerAvg e g`, `measurable_kerAvg`
  (`extSigma {e}`-measurable), `condExp_kerAvg` (`μ[g | extSigma {e}] = kerAvg e g` a.e.),
  `wilsonP_kerAvg` (`P_{e} f = kerAvg e g` a.e. when `f = g` a.e.), `kerAvg_update_self`;
  continuity `continuous_kerAvg` for a compact first-countable topological group whose open sets
  are measurable, and continuous `χ`, `g`.
* Block version for any link set `V`: `kerAvgV V g` (integral over the full product `∏ h`, of which
  only the coordinates in `V` are used), `measurable_kerAvgV`, `condExp_kerAvgV`, `wilsonP_kerAvgV`,
  `kerAvgV_blockUpd`, `continuous_kerAvgV` (compact second-countable topological group).
* SU(2) on `(ℤ/2Mℤ)⁴`, `μ ∝ exp((β/2) ∑ₚ Re tr U_p) ∏ dU`, every `M ≥ 1`, every real `β`, every
  continuous `g`: `su2_continuous_kerAvg`, `su2_condExp_kerAvg`, `su2_linkPj_kerAvg`,
  `su2_continuous_kerAvgV`, `su2_condExp_kerAvgV`, `su2_wilsonPj_kerAvgV`, and the corollaries
  `su2_linkPj_continuous_version`, `su2_wilsonPj_continuous_version` (`P_{e}` and `P_V` map elements
  of `H` with a continuous version to elements with a continuous version).

## (c) What remains open

These are exact finite-volume identities (the conditional law of one link and of one block); no
estimate is proved here. The oscillation bounds of the log-densities and the influence steps that
combine these kernels with Part XXVI's `kernel_infl` are not part of this module, and neither are
the continuous versions, oscillation functionals and density statements on `H`.

## (d) Axioms and checks

Only `propext`, `Classical.choice` and `Quot.sound` (the module axiom audit covers every headline);
no sorry, admit, axiom declarations, native_decide or implemented_by, and no `set_option`. Uses
Parts I, III, IV, VI, X and XXIX of this file.

## (e) Scope

This is not a proof of a mass gap, and no estimate is proved. It identifies the heat-bath
(Gibbs-sampler) kernels of the finite-volume Wilson measure: the conditional law of one link or
of one block given all other links, exactly and at every real coupling (for SU(2), `κ = β/2`
with `β = β_W = 4/g²`). These kernels define a Monte Carlo (heat-bath) dynamics, not the transfer
matrix, and nothing here bounds a gap of either; there is no infinite-volume or continuum
statement.
-/

namespace YangMills.StrongCoupling.HeatBathKernel

open MeasureTheory MeasureTheory.Measure SchurSplit YangMills.StrongCoupling.CubeSplit
  YangMills.StrongCoupling.CondExpInputs YangMills.StrongCoupling.WilsonCube

/-! ## The resampling engine -/

section Engine

variable {Ω Ξ : Type*} {m : MeasurableSpace Ω} [mΩ : MeasurableSpace Ω] [MeasurableSpace Ξ]

/-- An integral against a tilted measure as a ratio of two integrals. -/
theorem integral_tilted_eq_div (ρ : Measure Ξ) (ψ F : Ξ → ℝ) :
    ∫ ξ, F ξ ∂(ρ.tilted ψ) = (∫ ξ, Real.exp (ψ ξ) * F ξ ∂ρ) / ∫ ξ, Real.exp (ψ ξ) ∂ρ := by
  rw [integral_tilted, ← integral_div]
  congr 1
  funext ξ
  rw [smul_eq_mul, div_mul_eq_mul_div]

theorem integrable_exp_of_bound (ρ : Measure Ξ) [IsFiniteMeasure ρ] {ψ : Ξ → ℝ}
    (hψ : Measurable ψ) {B : ℝ} (hB : ∀ ξ, |ψ ξ| ≤ B) : Integrable (fun ξ => Real.exp (ψ ξ)) ρ :=
  (integrable_const (Real.exp B)).mono' hψ.exp.aestronglyMeasurable
    (ae_of_all _ fun ξ => by
      rw [Real.norm_eq_abs, Real.abs_exp]
      exact Real.exp_le_exp.2 ((le_abs_self _).trans (hB ξ)))

/-- An average against a tilted probability measure is bounded by a bound of the integrand. -/
theorem abs_integral_tilted_le (ρ : Measure Ξ) [IsProbabilityMeasure ρ] {ψ F : Ξ → ℝ}
    (hψ : Measurable ψ) {B : ℝ} (hB : ∀ ξ, |ψ ξ| ≤ B) {C : ℝ} (hC : ∀ ξ, |F ξ| ≤ C) :
    |∫ ξ, F ξ ∂(ρ.tilted ψ)| ≤ C := by
  have := isProbabilityMeasure_tilted (integrable_exp_of_bound ρ hψ hB)
  have h1 : ‖∫ ξ, F ξ ∂(ρ.tilted ψ)‖ ≤ C * (ρ.tilted ψ).real Set.univ :=
    norm_integral_le_of_norm_le_const (ae_of_all _ fun ξ => by rw [Real.norm_eq_abs]; exact hC ξ)
  rw [Real.norm_eq_abs, probReal_univ, mul_one] at h1
  exact h1

/-- A set integral against `ν₀.tilted w` as an integral against `ν₀`. -/
theorem setIntegral_tilted_eq (ν0 : Measure Ω) (w F : Ω → ℝ) {s : Set Ω} (hs : MeasurableSet s) :
    ∫ x in s, F x ∂(ν0.tilted w) =
      (∫ x, s.indicator F x * Real.exp (w x) ∂ν0) / ∫ x, Real.exp (w x) ∂ν0 := by
  rw [← integral_indicator hs, integral_tilted, ← integral_div]
  congr 1
  funext x
  rw [smul_eq_mul, div_mul_eq_mul_div, mul_comm]

variable (ν0 : Measure Ω) [IsProbabilityMeasure ν0] (ρ : Measure Ξ) [IsProbabilityMeasure ρ]
  {R : Ω × Ξ → Ω}

/-- **The exchange identity.** If `R` pushes `ν₀ ⊗ ρ` to `ν₀` and `H` is invariant under `R`, then
`∫ H Ψ dν₀ = ∫ H(U) ∫ Ψ(R(U, ξ)) dρ(ξ) dν₀(U)` for bounded measurable `H`, `Ψ`. -/
theorem integral_mul_resample (hR : Measurable R) (hmap : (ν0.prod ρ).map R = ν0)
    {H Ψ : Ω → ℝ} (hH : Measurable H) (hΨ : Measurable Ψ) {CH CΨ : ℝ}
    (hHb : ∀ U, |H U| ≤ CH) (hΨb : ∀ U, |Ψ U| ≤ CΨ) (hinv : ∀ U ξ, H (R (U, ξ)) = H U) :
    ∫ U, H U * Ψ U ∂ν0 = ∫ U, H U * ∫ ξ, Ψ (R (U, ξ)) ∂ρ ∂ν0 := by
  have hint : Integrable (fun p : Ω × Ξ => H p.1 * Ψ (R p)) (ν0.prod ρ) := by
    refine Integrable.of_bound ((hH.comp measurable_fst).mul (hΨ.comp hR)).aestronglyMeasurable
      (CH * CΨ) (ae_of_all _ fun p => ?_)
    rw [Real.norm_eq_abs, abs_mul]
    exact mul_le_mul (hHb _) (hΨb _) (abs_nonneg _) ((abs_nonneg _).trans (hHb p.1))
  calc ∫ U, H U * Ψ U ∂ν0 = ∫ U, H U * Ψ U ∂((ν0.prod ρ).map R) := by rw [hmap]
    _ = ∫ p, H (R p) * Ψ (R p) ∂(ν0.prod ρ) :=
        integral_map hR.aemeasurable (hH.mul hΨ).aestronglyMeasurable
    _ = ∫ p, H p.1 * Ψ (R p) ∂(ν0.prod ρ) := by
        congr 1
        funext p
        rw [show H (R p) = H p.1 from hinv p.1 p.2]
    _ = ∫ U, ∫ ξ, H U * Ψ (R (U, ξ)) ∂ρ ∂ν0 := integral_prod _ hint
    _ = ∫ U, H U * ∫ ξ, Ψ (R (U, ξ)) ∂ρ ∂ν0 := by
        congr 1
        funext U
        exact integral_const_mul _ _

omit [IsProbabilityMeasure ν0] in
/-- The kernel average is measurable. -/
theorem measurable_kernel (hR : Measurable R) {w g : Ω → ℝ} (hw : Measurable w)
    (hg : Measurable g) :
    Measurable fun U => ∫ ξ, g (R (U, ξ)) ∂(ρ.tilted fun ξ => w (R (U, ξ))) := by
  have hK : (fun U => ∫ ξ, g (R (U, ξ)) ∂(ρ.tilted fun ξ => w (R (U, ξ)))) = fun U =>
      (∫ ξ, Real.exp (w (R (U, ξ))) * g (R (U, ξ)) ∂ρ) / ∫ ξ, Real.exp (w (R (U, ξ))) ∂ρ :=
    funext fun U => integral_tilted_eq_div ρ _ _
  rw [hK]
  have h1 : Measurable fun p : Ω × Ξ => Real.exp (w (R p)) * g (R p) :=
    (hw.comp hR).exp.mul (hg.comp hR)
  have h2 : Measurable fun p : Ω × Ξ => Real.exp (w (R p)) := (hw.comp hR).exp
  exact h1.stronglyMeasurable.integral_prod_right'.measurable.div
    h2.stronglyMeasurable.integral_prod_right'.measurable

omit mΩ [IsProbabilityMeasure ν0] [IsProbabilityMeasure ρ] in
theorem kernel_congr {U U' : Ω} (hU : ∀ ξ, R (U, ξ) = R (U', ξ)) (w g : Ω → ℝ) :
    ∫ ξ, g (R (U, ξ)) ∂(ρ.tilted fun ξ => w (R (U, ξ))) =
      ∫ ξ, g (R (U', ξ)) ∂(ρ.tilted fun ξ => w (R (U', ξ))) := by
  simp only [hU]

/-- **The conditional expectation of a tilted measure under a resampling.** Let `R : Ω × Ξ → Ω`
push `ν₀ ⊗ ρ` to `ν₀` and factor through `pr` (`R(pr U, ξ) = R(U, ξ)`, `pr(R(U, ξ)) = pr U`), and let
`m = σ(pr)`. Then for bounded measurable `w`, `g`, `E_{ν₀.tilted w}[g | m]` is, almost everywhere,
the average of `g ∘ R(U, ·)` against `ρ` tilted by `w ∘ R(U, ·)`. -/
theorem condExp_resample (hm : m ≤ mΩ) {pr : Ω → Ω}
    (hprm : Measurable[m, mΩ] pr) (hmpr : m ≤ MeasurableSpace.comap pr mΩ)
    (hR : Measurable R) (hmap : (ν0.prod ρ).map R = ν0)
    (hprR : ∀ U ξ, pr (R (U, ξ)) = pr U) (hRpr : ∀ U ξ, R (pr U, ξ) = R (U, ξ))
    {w : Ω → ℝ} (hw : Measurable w) {B : ℝ} (hB : ∀ U, |w U| ≤ B)
    {g : Ω → ℝ} (hg : Measurable g) {C : ℝ} (hC : ∀ U, |g U| ≤ C) :
    (ν0.tilted w)[g | m] =ᵐ[ν0.tilted w]
      fun U => ∫ ξ, g (R (U, ξ)) ∂(ρ.tilted fun ξ => w (R (U, ξ))) := by
  have : IsProbabilityMeasure (ν0.tilted w) :=
    isProbabilityMeasure_tilted (integrable_exp_of_bound ν0 hw hB)
  obtain ⟨K, hKdef⟩ : ∃ K : Ω → ℝ,
      K = fun U => ∫ ξ, g (R (U, ξ)) ∂(ρ.tilted fun ξ => w (R (U, ξ))) := ⟨_, rfl⟩
  rw [← hKdef]
  have hwR : ∀ U, Measurable fun ξ => w (R (U, ξ)) := fun U =>
    hw.comp (hR.comp measurable_prodMk_left)
  have hKmeas : Measurable K := by
    rw [hKdef]
    exact measurable_kernel ρ hR hw hg
  have hKb : ∀ U, |K U| ≤ C := fun U => by
    rw [hKdef]
    exact abs_integral_tilted_le ρ (hwR U) (fun ξ => hB _) (fun ξ => hC _)
  have hKpr : ∀ U, K (pr U) = K U := fun U => by
    rw [hKdef]
    exact kernel_congr ρ (hRpr U) w g
  have hKR : ∀ U ξ, K (R (U, ξ)) = K U := fun U ξ => by
    rw [hKdef]
    exact kernel_congr ρ (fun ξ' => by rw [← hRpr (R (U, ξ)) ξ', hprR U ξ, hRpr U ξ']) w g
  have hKm : Measurable[m] K := by
    have hc : K = K ∘ pr := funext fun U => (hKpr U).symm
    rw [hc]
    exact hKmeas.comp hprm
  have hsinv : ∀ s, MeasurableSet[m] s → ∀ U ξ, R (U, ξ) ∈ s ↔ U ∈ s := by
    intro s hs U ξ
    obtain ⟨t, -, rfl⟩ := MeasurableSpace.measurableSet_comap.1 (hmpr s hs)
    simp only [Set.mem_preimage, hprR]
  have hD : ∀ U, 0 < ∫ ξ, Real.exp (w (R (U, ξ))) ∂ρ := fun U =>
    integral_exp_pos (integrable_exp_of_bound ρ (hwR U) fun ξ => hB _)
  have hCabs : ∀ U, |g U| ≤ |C| := fun U => (hC U).trans (le_abs_self C)
  refine (ae_eq_condExp_of_forall_setIntegral_eq hm ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_).symm
  · exact Integrable.of_bound hg.aestronglyMeasurable C
      (ae_of_all _ fun U => by rw [Real.norm_eq_abs]; exact hC U)
  · intro s _ _
    exact (Integrable.of_bound hKmeas.aestronglyMeasurable C
      (ae_of_all _ fun U => by rw [Real.norm_eq_abs]; exact hKb U)).integrableOn
  · intro s hs _
    have hs0 : MeasurableSet s := hm s hs
    rw [setIntegral_tilted_eq ν0 w K hs0, setIntegral_tilted_eq ν0 w g hs0]
    congr 1
    have hexpb : ∀ U, |Real.exp (w U)| ≤ Real.exp B := fun U => by
      rw [Real.abs_exp]
      exact Real.exp_le_exp.2 ((le_abs_self _).trans (hB U))
    have h1 := integral_mul_resample ν0 ρ hR hmap (hKmeas.indicator hs0) hw.exp
      (CH := |C|) (fun U => by
        by_cases hU : U ∈ s
        · rw [Set.indicator_of_mem hU]
          exact (hKb U).trans (le_abs_self C)
        · rw [Set.indicator_of_notMem hU, abs_zero]
          exact abs_nonneg C) hexpb
      (fun U ξ => by
        by_cases hU : U ∈ s
        · rw [Set.indicator_of_mem hU, Set.indicator_of_mem ((hsinv s hs U ξ).2 hU), hKR]
        · rw [Set.indicator_of_notMem hU,
            Set.indicator_of_notMem fun h' => hU ((hsinv s hs U ξ).1 h')])
    have h2 := integral_mul_resample ν0 ρ hR hmap (H := s.indicator fun _ => (1 : ℝ))
      (Ψ := fun U => g U * Real.exp (w U)) (measurable_const.indicator hs0) (hg.mul hw.exp)
      (CH := 1) (CΨ := |C| * Real.exp B) (fun U => by
        by_cases hU : U ∈ s
        · rw [Set.indicator_of_mem hU, abs_one]
        · rw [Set.indicator_of_notMem hU, abs_zero]
          exact zero_le_one) (fun U => by
        rw [abs_mul]
        exact mul_le_mul (hCabs U) (hexpb U) (abs_nonneg _) (abs_nonneg _))
      (fun U ξ => by
        by_cases hU : U ∈ s
        · rw [Set.indicator_of_mem hU, Set.indicator_of_mem ((hsinv s hs U ξ).2 hU)]
        · rw [Set.indicator_of_notMem hU,
            Set.indicator_of_notMem fun h' => hU ((hsinv s hs U ξ).1 h')])
    have h3 : ∫ U, s.indicator g U * Real.exp (w U) ∂ν0 =
        ∫ U, s.indicator (fun _ => (1 : ℝ)) U * (g U * Real.exp (w U)) ∂ν0 := by
      congr 1
      funext U
      by_cases hU : U ∈ s
      · rw [Set.indicator_of_mem hU, Set.indicator_of_mem hU, one_mul]
      · rw [Set.indicator_of_notMem hU, Set.indicator_of_notMem hU, zero_mul, zero_mul]
    rw [h1, h3, h2]
    congr 1
    funext U
    by_cases hU : U ∈ s
    · rw [Set.indicator_of_mem hU, Set.indicator_of_mem hU, one_mul, hKdef]
      dsimp only
      rw [integral_tilted_eq_div ρ, div_mul_cancel₀ _ (hD U).ne']
      congr 1
      funext ξ
      rw [mul_comm]
    · rw [Set.indicator_of_notMem hU, Set.indicator_of_notMem hU, zero_mul, zero_mul]
  · exact hKm.stronglyMeasurable.aestronglyMeasurable

omit [IsProbabilityMeasure ν0] in
/-- The kernel average is `σ(pr)`-measurable. -/
theorem measurable_kernel_of_pr {pr : Ω → Ω}
    (hprm : Measurable[m, mΩ] pr) (hR : Measurable R)
    (hRpr : ∀ U ξ, R (pr U, ξ) = R (U, ξ)) {w g : Ω → ℝ} (hw : Measurable w) (hg : Measurable g) :
    Measurable[m] fun U => ∫ ξ, g (R (U, ξ)) ∂(ρ.tilted fun ξ => w (R (U, ξ))) := by
  have hc : (fun U => ∫ ξ, g (R (U, ξ)) ∂(ρ.tilted fun ξ => w (R (U, ξ)))) =
      (fun U => ∫ ξ, g (R (U, ξ)) ∂(ρ.tilted fun ξ => w (R (U, ξ)))) ∘ pr :=
    funext fun U => kernel_congr ρ (fun ξ => (hRpr U ξ).symm) w g
  rw [hc]
  exact (measurable_kernel ρ hR hw hg).comp hprm

end Engine

/-! ## Updating a block of links -/

section Block

variable {E G : Type*}

open Classical in
/-- `U` updated on `V` by `W`: `W i` for `i ∈ V`, `U i` otherwise. -/
noncomputable def blockUpd (V : Set E) (W U : E → G) : E → G := fun i => if i ∈ V then W i else U i

theorem blockUpd_of_mem {V : Set E} {i : E} (hi : i ∈ V) (W U : E → G) :
    blockUpd V W U i = W i := by
  unfold blockUpd
  exact if_pos hi

theorem blockUpd_of_not_mem {V : Set E} {i : E} (hi : i ∉ V) (W U : E → G) :
    blockUpd V W U i = U i := by
  unfold blockUpd
  exact if_neg hi

theorem blockUpd_blockUpd (V : Set E) (W W' U : E → G) :
    blockUpd V W (blockUpd V W' U) = blockUpd V W U := by
  funext i
  by_cases hi : i ∈ V
  · rw [blockUpd_of_mem hi, blockUpd_of_mem hi]
  · rw [blockUpd_of_not_mem hi, blockUpd_of_not_mem hi, blockUpd_of_not_mem hi]

theorem blockUpd_left_blockUpd (V : Set E) (W W' U : E → G) :
    blockUpd V W' (blockUpd V W U) = blockUpd V W' U := blockUpd_blockUpd V W' W U

theorem blockUpd_update [DecidableEq E] (e : E) (W U : E → G) (s : G) :
    blockUpd ({e} : Set E) W (Function.update U e s) = blockUpd {e} W U := by
  funext i
  by_cases hi : i ∈ ({e} : Set E)
  · rw [blockUpd_of_mem hi, blockUpd_of_mem hi]
  · rw [blockUpd_of_not_mem hi, blockUpd_of_not_mem hi,
      Function.update_of_ne fun h' => hi (Set.mem_singleton_iff.2 h')]

theorem update_blockUpd [DecidableEq E] (e : E) (W U : E → G) (s : G) :
    Function.update (blockUpd ({e} : Set E) W U) e s = Function.update U e s := by
  funext i
  by_cases hi : i = e
  · subst hi
    rw [Function.update_self, Function.update_self]
  · rw [Function.update_of_ne hi, Function.update_of_ne hi,
      blockUpd_of_not_mem fun h' => hi (Set.mem_singleton_iff.1 h')]

variable [MeasurableSpace G]

theorem measurable_blockUpd (V : Set E) :
    Measurable fun p : (E → G) × (E → G) => blockUpd V p.2 p.1 := by
  refine measurable_pi_lambda _ fun i => ?_
  by_cases hi : i ∈ V
  · have hc : (fun p : (E → G) × (E → G) => blockUpd V p.2 p.1 i) = fun p => p.2 i :=
      funext fun p => blockUpd_of_mem hi _ _
    rw [hc]
    exact (measurable_pi_apply i).comp measurable_snd
  · have hc : (fun p : (E → G) × (E → G) => blockUpd V p.2 p.1 i) = fun p => p.1 i :=
      funext fun p => blockUpd_of_not_mem hi _ _
    rw [hc]
    exact (measurable_pi_apply i).comp measurable_fst

/-- `U ↦ blockUpd V 1 U` is measurable for the exterior σ-algebra of `V`. -/
theorem measurable_blockUpd_extSigma [One G] (V : Set E) :
    Measurable[extSigma (G := G) V] (blockUpd V (1 : E → G)) := by
  refine @measurable_pi_lambda _ _ _ (extSigma V) _ _ fun i => ?_
  by_cases hi : i ∈ V
  · have hc : (fun U : E → G => blockUpd V 1 U i) = fun _ => (1 : G) :=
      funext fun U => blockUpd_of_mem hi _ _
    rw [hc]
    exact measurable_const
  · have hc : (fun U : E → G => blockUpd V 1 U i) = fun U => U i :=
      funext fun U => blockUpd_of_not_mem hi _ _
    rw [hc]
    exact YangMills.StrongCoupling.FibreReduction.measurable_eval_extSigma hi

/-- The exterior σ-algebra of `V` is contained in the σ-algebra generated by `U ↦ blockUpd V 1 U`
(with `measurable_blockUpd_extSigma`, the two are equal). -/
theorem extSigma_le_comap_blockUpd [One G] (V : Set E) :
    extSigma (G := G) V ≤ MeasurableSpace.comap (blockUpd V (1 : E → G)) MeasurableSpace.pi := by
  refine iSup₂_le fun i hi => ?_
  have hi' : i ∉ V := hi
  rw [← measurable_iff_comap_le]
  have hc : (fun U : E → G => U i) = (fun U : E → G => U i) ∘ blockUpd V 1 :=
    funext fun U => (blockUpd_of_not_mem hi' 1 U).symm
  rw [hc]
  exact (measurable_pi_apply i).comp (comap_measurable _)

variable [Fintype E] (h : Measure G) [IsProbabilityMeasure h]

/-- **Block resampling preserves the product measure `∏ h`**: `(U, W) ↦ blockUpd V W U` pushes
`(∏ h) ⊗ (∏ h)` to `∏ h`. -/
theorem map_blockUpd (V : Set E) :
    ((Measure.pi fun _ : E => h).prod (Measure.pi fun _ : E => h)).map
      (fun p : (E → G) × (E → G) => blockUpd V p.2 p.1) = Measure.pi fun _ : E => h := by
  refine (Measure.pi_eq fun s hs => ?_).symm
  rw [Measure.map_apply (measurable_blockUpd V) (MeasurableSet.univ_pi hs)]
  have hpre : (fun p : (E → G) × (E → G) => blockUpd V p.2 p.1) ⁻¹' Set.univ.pi s =
      Set.univ.pi (blockUpd V (fun _ => Set.univ) s) ×ˢ
        Set.univ.pi (blockUpd V s fun _ => Set.univ) := by
    ext ⟨U, W⟩
    simp only [Set.mem_preimage, Set.mem_prod, Set.mem_univ_pi]
    constructor
    · intro hx
      refine ⟨fun i => ?_, fun i => ?_⟩
      · by_cases hi : i ∈ V
        · rw [blockUpd_of_mem hi]
          exact Set.mem_univ _
        · have h1 := hx i
          rw [blockUpd_of_not_mem hi] at h1 ⊢
          exact h1
      · by_cases hi : i ∈ V
        · have h1 := hx i
          rw [blockUpd_of_mem hi] at h1 ⊢
          exact h1
        · rw [blockUpd_of_not_mem hi]
          exact Set.mem_univ _
    · rintro ⟨hU, hW⟩ i
      by_cases hi : i ∈ V
      · have h1 := hW i
        rw [blockUpd_of_mem hi] at h1 ⊢
        exact h1
      · have h1 := hU i
        rw [blockUpd_of_not_mem hi] at h1 ⊢
        exact h1
  rw [hpre, Measure.prod_prod, Measure.pi_pi, Measure.pi_pi, ← Finset.prod_mul_distrib]
  refine Finset.prod_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
  by_cases hi : i ∈ V
  · simp only [blockUpd_of_mem hi, measure_univ, one_mul]
  · simp only [blockUpd_of_not_mem hi, measure_univ, mul_one]

/-- **Single-link resampling preserves the product measure `∏ h`**: `(U, s) ↦ update U e s` pushes
`(∏ h) ⊗ h` to `∏ h`. -/
theorem map_update [DecidableEq E] (e : E) :
    ((Measure.pi fun _ : E => h).prod h).map (fun p : (E → G) × G => Function.update p.1 e p.2) =
      Measure.pi fun _ : E => h := by
  refine (Measure.pi_eq fun s hs => ?_).symm
  rw [Measure.map_apply measurable_update' (MeasurableSet.univ_pi hs)]
  have hpre : (fun p : (E → G) × G => Function.update p.1 e p.2) ⁻¹' Set.univ.pi s =
      Set.univ.pi (Function.update s e Set.univ) ×ˢ s e := by
    ext ⟨U, x⟩
    simp only [Set.mem_preimage, Set.mem_prod, Set.mem_univ_pi]
    constructor
    · intro hx
      refine ⟨fun i => ?_, ?_⟩
      · by_cases hi : i = e
        · subst hi
          rw [Function.update_self]
          exact Set.mem_univ _
        · have h1 := hx i
          rw [Function.update_of_ne hi] at h1 ⊢
          exact h1
      · have h1 := hx e
        rw [Function.update_self] at h1
        exact h1
    · rintro ⟨hU, hx⟩ i
      by_cases hi : i = e
      · subst hi
        rw [Function.update_self]
        exact hx
      · have h1 := hU i
        rw [Function.update_of_ne hi] at h1 ⊢
        exact h1
  rw [hpre, Measure.prod_prod, Measure.pi_pi, Fintype.prod_eq_mul_prod_compl e,
    Fintype.prod_eq_mul_prod_compl e (fun i => h (s i)), Function.update_self, measure_univ,
    one_mul, mul_comm]
  congr 1
  refine Finset.prod_congr rfl fun i hi => ?_
  have hne : i ≠ e := fun h' => (Finset.mem_compl.1 hi) (Finset.mem_singleton.2 h')
  rw [Function.update_of_ne hne]

end Block

/-! ## The heat-bath kernels of the Wilson measure -/

section Wilson

variable {S E G : Type*} [OrientedGraph S E] [Fintype E] [Group G] [MeasurableSpace G]
  [MeasurableMul₂ G] [MeasurableInv G]
  {Pl : Type*} [Fintype Pl] (plaq : Pl → Plaq S E) (χ : ClassFn G) (κ : ℝ)
  (h : Measure G) [IsProbabilityMeasure h]

/-- **The single-link heat-bath kernel**: the average of `g` over the link `e` against `h` tilted
by the Wilson exponent, the other links of `U` frozen. Physically, the heat-bath update of `e`:
only the plaquettes containing `e` depend on `s`; the others give a constant factor that the
normalisation of the tilt removes (for SU(2): the Boltzmann weight of `e` in the field of its
staples). That reduction is not stated or used here. -/
noncomputable def kerAvg [DecidableEq E] (e : E) (g : (E → G) → ℝ) (U : E → G) : ℝ :=
  ∫ s, g (Function.update U e s) ∂(h.tilted fun s => wilsonExp plaq χ κ (Function.update U e s))

/-- **The block heat-bath kernel**: the average of `g` over the links of `V` against the
product measure `∏ h` tilted by the Wilson exponent, the links of `U` outside `V` frozen. -/
noncomputable def kerAvgV (V : Set E) (g : (E → G) → ℝ) (U : E → G) : ℝ :=
  ∫ W, g (blockUpd V W U) ∂((Measure.pi fun _ : E => h).tilted fun W =>
    wilsonExp plaq χ κ (blockUpd V W U))

omit [Fintype E] [MeasurableMul₂ G] [MeasurableInv G] [IsProbabilityMeasure h] in
/-- `kerAvg e g` does not depend on the value `U e` of the resampled link `e`. -/
theorem kerAvg_update_self [DecidableEq E] (e : E) (g : (E → G) → ℝ) (U : E → G) (s : G) :
    kerAvg plaq χ κ h e g (Function.update U e s) = kerAvg plaq χ κ h e g U := by
  unfold kerAvg
  simp only [Function.update_idem]

omit [MeasurableMul₂ G] [MeasurableInv G] [IsProbabilityMeasure h] in
/-- `kerAvgV V g` does not depend on the values of `U` on the resampled links `V`. -/
theorem kerAvgV_blockUpd (V : Set E) (g : (E → G) → ℝ) (W U : E → G) :
    kerAvgV plaq χ κ h V g (blockUpd V W U) = kerAvgV plaq χ κ h V g U := by
  unfold kerAvgV
  simp only [blockUpd_blockUpd]

omit [Fintype E] in
/-- `kerAvg e g` is measurable for the σ-algebra of the links `≠ e`. -/
theorem measurable_kerAvg [DecidableEq E] (e : E) {g : (E → G) → ℝ} (hg : Measurable g) :
    Measurable[extSigma (G := G) ({e} : Set E)] (kerAvg plaq χ κ h e g) :=
  measurable_kernel_of_pr h (m := extSigma (G := G) ({e} : Set E))
    (R := fun p : (E → G) × G => Function.update p.1 e p.2) (pr := blockUpd ({e} : Set E) 1)
    (measurable_blockUpd_extSigma _) measurable_update' (fun U s => update_blockUpd e 1 U s)
    (measurable_wilsonExp plaq χ κ) hg

/-- `kerAvgV V g` is measurable for the σ-algebra of the links outside `V`. -/
theorem measurable_kerAvgV (V : Set E) {g : (E → G) → ℝ} (hg : Measurable g) :
    Measurable[extSigma (G := G) V] (kerAvgV plaq χ κ h V g) :=
  measurable_kernel_of_pr (Measure.pi fun _ : E => h)
    (m := extSigma (G := G) V) (R := fun p : (E → G) × (E → G) => blockUpd V p.2 p.1)
    (pr := blockUpd V 1)
    (measurable_blockUpd_extSigma V) (measurable_blockUpd V) (fun U W => blockUpd_blockUpd V W 1 U)
    (measurable_wilsonExp plaq χ κ) hg

/-- **The single-link heat-bath kernel formula** (generic Wilson setting): for bounded measurable
`g`, `E_μ[g | links ≠ e] = kerAvg e g` almost everywhere. -/
theorem condExp_kerAvg [DecidableEq E] (e : E) {g : (E → G) → ℝ} (hg : Measurable g) {C : ℝ}
    (hC : ∀ U, |g U| ≤ C) :
    (wilsonMeasure plaq χ κ h)[g | extSigma (G := G) ({e} : Set E)]
      =ᵐ[wilsonMeasure plaq χ κ h] kerAvg plaq χ κ h e g :=
  condExp_resample (Measure.pi fun _ : E => h) h
    (m := extSigma (G := G) ({e} : Set E)) (R := fun p : (E → G) × G => Function.update p.1 e p.2)
    (pr := blockUpd ({e} : Set E) 1) (extSigma_le _)
    (measurable_blockUpd_extSigma _) (extSigma_le_comap_blockUpd _) measurable_update'
    (map_update h e) (fun U s => blockUpd_update e 1 U s) (fun U s => update_blockUpd e 1 U s)
    (measurable_wilsonExp plaq χ κ) (abs_wilsonExp_le plaq χ κ) hg hC

/-- **The block heat-bath kernel formula** (generic Wilson setting, any link set `V`): for bounded
measurable `g`, `E_μ[g | links outside V] = kerAvgV V g` almost everywhere. -/
theorem condExp_kerAvgV (V : Set E) {g : (E → G) → ℝ} (hg : Measurable g) {C : ℝ}
    (hC : ∀ U, |g U| ≤ C) :
    (wilsonMeasure plaq χ κ h)[g | extSigma (G := G) V]
      =ᵐ[wilsonMeasure plaq χ κ h] kerAvgV plaq χ κ h V g :=
  condExp_resample (Measure.pi fun _ : E => h) (Measure.pi fun _ : E => h)
    (m := extSigma (G := G) V) (R := fun p : (E → G) × (E → G) => blockUpd V p.2 p.1)
    (pr := blockUpd V 1) (extSigma_le _)
    (measurable_blockUpd_extSigma V) (extSigma_le_comap_blockUpd V) (measurable_blockUpd V)
    (map_blockUpd h V) (fun U W => blockUpd_blockUpd V 1 W U)
    (fun U W => blockUpd_blockUpd V W 1 U)
    (measurable_wilsonExp plaq χ κ) (abs_wilsonExp_le plaq χ κ) hg hC

variable [IsMulLeftInvariant h] [IsMulRightInvariant h]

/-- **The single-link heat bath on `H`**: if `f ∈ H` has the bounded measurable version `g`, then
`P_{e} f = kerAvg e g` almost everywhere. -/
theorem wilsonP_kerAvg [DecidableEq E] (e : E) {g : (E → G) → ℝ} (hg : Measurable g) {C : ℝ}
    (hC : ∀ U, |g U| ≤ C) (f : wilsonH plaq χ κ h)
    (hf : ((f : Lp ℝ 2 (wilsonMeasure plaq χ κ h)) : (E → G) → ℝ) =ᵐ[wilsonMeasure plaq χ κ h] g) :
    (((wilsonP plaq χ κ h ({e} : Set E) f : wilsonH plaq χ κ h) :
      Lp ℝ 2 (wilsonMeasure plaq χ κ h)) : (E → G) → ℝ)
      =ᵐ[wilsonMeasure plaq χ κ h] kerAvg plaq χ κ h e g :=
  (condL2_ae_eq_condExp (wilsonMeasure plaq χ κ h) (extSigma_le _)
    (f : Lp ℝ 2 (wilsonMeasure plaq χ κ h))).trans
    ((condExp_congr_ae hf).trans (condExp_kerAvg plaq χ κ h e hg hC))

/-- **The block heat bath on `H`**: if `f ∈ H` has the bounded measurable version `g`, then
`P_V f = kerAvgV V g` almost everywhere. -/
theorem wilsonP_kerAvgV (V : Set E) {g : (E → G) → ℝ} (hg : Measurable g) {C : ℝ}
    (hC : ∀ U, |g U| ≤ C) (f : wilsonH plaq χ κ h)
    (hf : ((f : Lp ℝ 2 (wilsonMeasure plaq χ κ h)) : (E → G) → ℝ) =ᵐ[wilsonMeasure plaq χ κ h] g) :
    (((wilsonP plaq χ κ h V f : wilsonH plaq χ κ h) :
      Lp ℝ 2 (wilsonMeasure plaq χ κ h)) : (E → G) → ℝ)
      =ᵐ[wilsonMeasure plaq χ κ h] kerAvgV plaq χ κ h V g :=
  (condL2_ae_eq_condExp (wilsonMeasure plaq χ κ h) (extSigma_le _)
    (f : Lp ℝ 2 (wilsonMeasure plaq χ κ h))).trans
    ((condExp_congr_ae hf).trans (condExp_kerAvgV plaq χ κ h V hg hC))

end Wilson

/-! ## Continuity of the kernels for a compact group -/

section Continuity

variable {X Ξ : Type*} [TopologicalSpace X] [FirstCountableTopology X] [MeasurableSpace Ξ]

/-- **Continuity of a tilted average in a parameter** (first-countable parameter space; bounded
integrands and log-densities, each continuous in the parameter and measurable in `ξ`). -/
theorem continuous_tilted_average (ρ : Measure Ξ) [IsProbabilityMeasure ρ] {Φ ψ : X → Ξ → ℝ}
    (hΦ : ∀ ξ, Continuous fun x => Φ x ξ) (hψ : ∀ ξ, Continuous fun x => ψ x ξ)
    (hΦm : ∀ x, Measurable (Φ x)) (hψm : ∀ x, Measurable (ψ x)) {B C : ℝ}
    (hB : ∀ x ξ, |ψ x ξ| ≤ B) (hC : ∀ x ξ, |Φ x ξ| ≤ C) :
    Continuous fun x => ∫ ξ, Φ x ξ ∂(ρ.tilted (ψ x)) := by
  have hK : (fun x => ∫ ξ, Φ x ξ ∂(ρ.tilted (ψ x))) = fun x =>
      (∫ ξ, Real.exp (ψ x ξ) * Φ x ξ ∂ρ) / ∫ ξ, Real.exp (ψ x ξ) ∂ρ :=
    funext fun x => integral_tilted_eq_div ρ _ _
  rw [hK]
  have hexpb : ∀ x ξ, ‖Real.exp (ψ x ξ)‖ ≤ Real.exp B := fun x ξ => by
    rw [Real.norm_eq_abs, Real.abs_exp]
    exact Real.exp_le_exp.2 ((le_abs_self _).trans (hB x ξ))
  refine Continuous.div ?_ ?_ fun x =>
    (integral_exp_pos (integrable_exp_of_bound ρ (hψm x) (hB x))).ne'
  · refine continuous_of_dominated (bound := fun _ => Real.exp B * C)
      (fun x => ((hψm x).exp.mul (hΦm x)).aestronglyMeasurable)
      (fun x => ae_of_all _ fun ξ => ?_) (integrable_const _)
      (ae_of_all _ fun ξ => (hψ ξ).rexp.mul (hΦ ξ))
    rw [norm_mul, Real.norm_eq_abs (Φ x ξ)]
    exact mul_le_mul (hexpb x ξ) (hC x ξ) (abs_nonneg _) (Real.exp_pos B).le
  · exact continuous_of_dominated (bound := fun _ => Real.exp B)
      (fun x => (hψm x).exp.aestronglyMeasurable)
      (fun x => ae_of_all _ fun ξ => hexpb x ξ) (integrable_const _)
      (ae_of_all _ fun ξ => (hψ ξ).rexp)

end Continuity

section WilsonContinuity

variable {S E G : Type*} [OrientedGraph S E] [Fintype E] [Group G] [MeasurableSpace G]
  [MeasurableMul₂ G] [MeasurableInv G]
  {Pl : Type*} [Fintype Pl] (plaq : Pl → Plaq S E) (χ : ClassFn G) (κ : ℝ)
  (h : Measure G) [IsProbabilityMeasure h] [TopologicalSpace G] [IsTopologicalGroup G]

omit [Fintype E] [MeasurableSpace G] [MeasurableMul₂ G] [MeasurableInv G] in
theorem continuous_hol_gen (p : Plaq S E) : Continuous (hol p : (E → G) → G) := by
  have hc : (hol p : (E → G) → G) = fun U => U p.l1 * U p.l2 * (U p.l3)⁻¹ * (U p.l4)⁻¹ := rfl
  rw [hc]
  exact (((continuous_apply p.l1).mul (continuous_apply p.l2)).mul
    (continuous_apply p.l3).inv).mul (continuous_apply p.l4).inv

omit [Fintype E] [MeasurableMul₂ G] [MeasurableInv G] in
/-- The Wilson exponent is continuous when `χ` is. -/
theorem continuous_wilsonExp_of (hχ : Continuous χ.toFun) : Continuous (wilsonExp plaq χ κ) := by
  have hc : wilsonExp plaq χ κ = fun U => κ * ∑ p, χ.toFun (hol (plaq p) U) := rfl
  rw [hc]
  exact continuous_const.mul
    (continuous_finsetSum _ fun p _ => hχ.comp (continuous_hol_gen (plaq p)))

omit [Fintype E] [Group G] [MeasurableSpace G] [MeasurableMul₂ G] [MeasurableInv G]
  [IsTopologicalGroup G] in
theorem continuous_blockUpd (V : Set E) :
    Continuous fun p : (E → G) × (E → G) => blockUpd V p.2 p.1 := by
  refine continuous_pi fun i => ?_
  by_cases hi : i ∈ V
  · have hc : (fun p : (E → G) × (E → G) => blockUpd V p.2 p.1 i) = fun p => p.2 i :=
      funext fun p => blockUpd_of_mem hi _ _
    rw [hc]
    exact (continuous_apply i).comp continuous_snd
  · have hc : (fun p : (E → G) × (E → G) => blockUpd V p.2 p.1 i) = fun p => p.1 i :=
      funext fun p => blockUpd_of_not_mem hi _ _
    rw [hc]
    exact (continuous_apply i).comp continuous_fst

omit [Fintype E] [Group G] [MeasurableSpace G] [MeasurableMul₂ G] [MeasurableInv G]
  [IsTopologicalGroup G] in
theorem exists_abs_le_of_continuous [CompactSpace G] {g : (E → G) → ℝ} (hg : Continuous g) :
    ∃ C, ∀ U, |g U| ≤ C := by
  obtain ⟨C, hC⟩ := isCompact_univ.exists_bound_of_continuousOn hg.continuousOn
  exact ⟨C, fun U => by
    have h1 := hC U (Set.mem_univ U)
    rwa [Real.norm_eq_abs] at h1⟩

omit [MeasurableMul₂ G] [MeasurableInv G] in
/-- **Continuity of the single-link kernel** (compact first-countable topological group, continuous
`χ` and `g`). -/
theorem continuous_kerAvg [DecidableEq E] [CompactSpace G] [OpensMeasurableSpace G]
    [FirstCountableTopology G] (hχ : Continuous χ.toFun) (e : E) {g : (E → G) → ℝ}
    (hg : Continuous g) : Continuous (kerAvg plaq χ κ h e g) := by
  obtain ⟨C, hC⟩ := exists_abs_le_of_continuous hg
  have hw := continuous_wilsonExp_of plaq χ κ hχ
  have h1 : ∀ s : G, Continuous fun U : E → G => Function.update U e s := fun s =>
    continuous_id.update e continuous_const
  have h2 : ∀ U : E → G, Continuous fun s : G => Function.update U e s := fun U =>
    continuous_const.update e continuous_id
  exact continuous_tilted_average h (Φ := fun U s => g (Function.update U e s))
    (ψ := fun U s => wilsonExp plaq χ κ (Function.update U e s))
    (fun s => hg.comp (h1 s)) (fun s => hw.comp (h1 s))
    (fun U => (hg.comp (h2 U)).measurable) (fun U => (hw.comp (h2 U)).measurable)
    (fun U s => abs_wilsonExp_le plaq χ κ _) (fun U s => hC _)

omit [MeasurableMul₂ G] [MeasurableInv G] in
/-- **Continuity of the block kernel** (compact second-countable topological group, continuous `χ`
and `g`, any link set `V`). -/
theorem continuous_kerAvgV [CompactSpace G] [OpensMeasurableSpace G] [SecondCountableTopology G]
    (hχ : Continuous χ.toFun) (V : Set E) {g : (E → G) → ℝ} (hg : Continuous g) :
    Continuous (kerAvgV plaq χ κ h V g) := by
  obtain ⟨C, hC⟩ := exists_abs_le_of_continuous hg
  have hw := continuous_wilsonExp_of plaq χ κ hχ
  have h1 : ∀ W : E → G, Continuous fun U : E → G => blockUpd V W U := fun W =>
    (continuous_blockUpd V).comp (continuous_id.prodMk continuous_const)
  have h2 : ∀ U : E → G, Continuous fun W : E → G => blockUpd V W U := fun U =>
    (continuous_blockUpd V).comp (continuous_const.prodMk continuous_id)
  exact continuous_tilted_average (Measure.pi fun _ : E => h)
    (Φ := fun U W => g (blockUpd V W U)) (ψ := fun U W => wilsonExp plaq χ κ (blockUpd V W U))
    (fun W => hg.comp (h1 W)) (fun W => hw.comp (h1 W))
    (fun U => (hg.comp (h2 U)).measurable) (fun U => (hw.comp (h2 U)).measurable)
    (fun U W => abs_wilsonExp_le plaq χ κ _) (fun U W => hC _)

end WilsonContinuity

